{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion","id":740377,"title":"Werewolf Gifts - 2e Conversion","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-29T18:12:12-07:00","id":740377,"title":"Werewolf Gifts - 2e Conversion","content":"Seeing as Werewolf 2e players have a shortage of official Moon Gifts as well as Gifts tied to the Pure, I'm putting up this thread for those interested in converting some of the Gifts from the 1e books into the 2e system. That said, I'll start off with the Wolfslayer Gift (which, naturally, is a Wolf Gift). More revisions will be made as I familiarize myself more with the Facet mechanics.<br /> <br /> <b>EDIT: </b>This is also going to be the thread where I'll be posting any original Gifts on, as well. <hr /><span style=\"font-size:26px\"><u><b>Gift of the Wolfslayer</b></u></span><br /> <br /> The Facets of the Wolfslayer Gift are powers only effective against werewolves, and almost always harmful or negative. Scholars among the Forsaken and Pure believe them to be a legacy of Father Wolf's death, another punishment to his half-spirit children for their crime. Whatever its origins, most Uratha in the Tribes of the Moon recognize the danger of its abuse, and discourage their peers from learning the Gift on the risk of violating the Oath. The Blood Talons are the exception, though, with their favored prey, and many among them develop the Gift's Facets to more efficiently hunt other werewolves. Meanwhile, the Pure do not hold as strong a stigma towards the Gift, and will happily use it to lethal effect against their Forsaken cousins. Members of the Fire-Touched are especially likely to develop a few Facets.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Patronless Pack</u> [Cunning]</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Essence<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Intelligence + Occult + Cunning - Totem's Resistance<br /> <b>Action: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Cunning Hours<br /> Nearly every werewolf pack has a personal and specific totem, which lends them a portion of its power in exchange for children among the Uratha. Werewolves with this Gift can temporarily sever the bond between pack and totem, eliminating some of the advantages her enemies have.<br /> <br /> <u>Dramatic Failure:</u> Offended by the attempt, the spirits instead separate the werewolf from her totem for one day.<br /> <br /> <u>Failure:</u> The werewolf is unable to remove the influence of her opponents' Totem's.<br /> <br /> <u>Success:</u> The werewolf targets a pack and temporarily drives a wedge between them and their totem. They lose any and all totem benefits for a number of hours equal to the character's Cunning Renown. She affects all werewolves she can see that belong to the same pack; she need not know the pack's name to target it -- looking at an enemy werewolf and concentrating on that pack is enough. Members of the affected pack not present are unaffected by the Gift and remain blessed by the totem. Some werewolves consider being under the effect of this Gift to free them from the constraints of their totem's ban until the Gift ends, but few totem spirits see it that way.<br /> <br /> <u>Exceptional Success:</u> The sundering of the pack's connection to its totem is absolute. Even members of the pack who are not present at the Facet's activation are cut off from the spirit.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Object Of Piercing Clarity</u> [Glory]</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Essence<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Presence + Expression + Glory vs. Composure + Primal Urge<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Glory Hours<br /> One of the People's greatest defenses is Lunacy. Against mortals, it is usually effective enough to end a fight. When the fight is with other supernaturals, Lunacy can blank the minds of those annoying witnesses. It may be hard to deal with in personal life, but it's a great blessing when worrying about &quot;the herd,&quot; especially when a war spills into the streets. This frightening Gift frees a werewolf from the curse of Lunacy for a time. While it may seem like a boon for those Uratha who still try to live a human life, it is definitely a double-edged sword.<br /> <br /> <u>Dramatic Failure:</u> The Gift's effects twist and rebound on the character, amplifying the Lunacy he radiates to others. For a number of days equal to 6 - (the number of dots away from Harmony 5), the character inflicts mild Lunacy in Hishu or Urhan Form, and full Lunacy in Dalu or Urshul Form. If he assumes Gauru form, all breaking point rolls resulting from Lunacy are made at a chance die.<br /> <br /> <u>Failure:</u> The Gift fails to dampen the target's cloak of Lunacy.<br /> <br /> <u>Success:</u> The werewolf temporarily subdues his target's Lunacy; the target senses this dampening. For the Facet's duration, any onlookers who see the target gain one automatic success on the associated breaking point roll<br /> <br /> A werewolf concerned with the Oath of the Moon might break off the fight and retreat, more wary of revealing herself than usual. Or the humans that see her in an impossible shape -- and recognize it, thanks to the Gift -- might assault her, especially if her opponent looks like nothing more than a fellow mortal. Use of this Gift can be very tactically effective, but many Uratha do not approve. It is a few hairs-breadths short of actively revealing the People to humanity, which no sane werewolf desires.<br /> <br /> <u>Exceptional Success:</u> The werewolf greatly weakens his target's Lunacy. All mortals who see the target only need three successes to score an exceptional success in the breaking point.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Discordant Form</u> [Honor]</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Essence<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Presence + Science + Honor vs. Resolve + Primal Urge<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Honor Minutes<br /> Shifting shape is instinctive to the People. It's as completely natural as clenching a fist or flipping off the guy who's tailing you. Even those who cleave more to Flesh can manage to make the transition with ease. Hence, a given Uratha can become frustrated - even panicked - if he finds that his ability to shapechange is either difficult to invoke, or barely controllable.<br /> <br /> <u>Dramatic Failure</u>: The Gift not only fails to affect the target, but rebounds on the werewolf who invoked it. The character suffers the effects of Discordant Form as if it scored a success.<br /> <br /> <u>Failure:</u> The Gift fails to affect the target's shapeshifting abilities.<br /> <br /> <u>Success:</u> Each success on the roll pushes the target werewolf's effective Harmony towards a direction of the character's choosing.<br /> <br /> <u>Exceptional Success:</u> As success, but the affected werewolf must spend a Willpower point when attempting to change shape.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Human Health</u> [Purity]</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Essence<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Wits + Medicine + Purity vs. Composure + Primal Urge<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> One of the Uratha's most serious advantages in battle is their ability to bounce back from nearly any wound, and quickly. Take that away, and a werewolf goes down that much faster. Even worse, a werewolf in Gauru knows he has to release the form soon or go berserk, and if he's taken so many wounds that he would die by shifting back to human, he's in a very bad place.<br /> <br /> <u>Dramatic Failure:</u> Rather than shutting down, the target's enhanced healing blurs into action. As if the werewolf spent a point of Essence on her target's behalf, the target immediately heals an amount of lethal damage according to his Primal Urge.<br /> <br /> <u>Failure:</u> The target continues to heal as normal.<br /> <br /> <u>Success:</u> For a number of hours equal to the character's Purity, the target heals as a human does. He cannot spend Essence to heal lethal wounds instantly, though it will heal bashing wounds. This power can end prematurely if the Werewolf falls into Basu-Im.<br /> <br /> <u>Exceptional Success:</u> The effect lasts a number of days equal to the character's Purity, and the target werewolf cannot even spend Essence to heal bashing damage.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Return To Birth</u> [Wisdom]</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Essence<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Manipulation + Science + Wisdom vs. Resolve + Primal Urge<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> Hishu, while the best form for hiding among the six billion sheep on Earth, is one of the least combat-effective and everyone knows it. This Gift forces a werewolf back into human form, though it can't keep her there.<br /> <br /> <u>Dramatic Failure:</u> The attempt fails, and the werewolf cannot use this Gift again for 24 hours<br /> .<br /> <u>Failure:</u> The werewolf fails to force his target into her human shape.<br /> <br /> <u>Success:</u> The target reverts immediately to Hishu form and cannot change shape for a number of turns equal to the werewolf's Wisdom Renown. For werewolves already suffering from Discordant Form, this forced change does not end that effect. A werewolf currently suffering Kuruth is immune to this Gift.<br /> <br /> <u>Exceptional Success:</u> The target's system is so shocked by being forced into Hishu form that she cannot attempt to change into another shape for a number of hours equal to the werewolf's Wisdom Renown.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 02-01-2016, 03:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T19:59:37-07:00","id":740681,"title":"","content":"Do remember that 2nd Edition shapechanging no longer requires a roll at all, so Form Lock might need to change to reflect that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T21:18:22-07:00","id":740796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=740681#post740681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do remember that 2nd Edition shapechanging no longer requires a roll at all, so Form Lock might need to change to reflect that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? Then, perhaps it could <i>impose</i> a roll to shapechanging? Or failing that, maybe force the werewolf to pay an additional cost in Essence or Willpower?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T03:26:57-07:00","id":741244,"title":"","content":"The simplest way of modelling it would be making them shift as though their harmony was higher. Like, numerically. At harmony 9 or 10 they need essence and an instant action, at 7 and 8 it's essence <i>or</i> an instant action, 4, 5 and 6 they can do it reflexively at will, and below 4 they have trouble <i>not</i> shifting in some circumstances.<br /> <br /> So you could have the gift shunt them [Honor] or [Successes] up the harmony chart for the purpose of changing form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T05:09:11-07:00","id":741396,"title":"","content":"Honor Renown could determine the Facet's effectiveness at pushing the target's effective Harmony up. Successes could dictate length. A normal success makes the Facet last for a proportionate number of turns. An exceptional success makes it last a scene.<br /> <br /> And to make it more versatile, perhaps Form Lock might allow for pushing a Werewolf's Harmony <i>down</i> for the purposes of shapeshifting? And perhaps change the name from Form Lock to something that evokes a mercurial tone?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 10-30-2015, 08:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T06:20:42-07:00","id":741560,"title":"","content":"It needs something. As it stands there's a good chance of it doing nothing at all, which is no good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T05:01:09-08:00","id":746380,"title":"","content":"Revised the Cunning Facet and added the Glory Facet to Wolfslayer. Critique is appreciated, as always.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T08:01:20-08:00","id":746617,"title":"","content":"On the Purity Facet, I think Basu-Im should end the facet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T13:12:13-08:00","id":747315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=746617#post746617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the Purity Facet, I think Basu-Im should end the facet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Noted it, and made the addition. Thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T13:17:53-08:00","id":747319,"title":"","content":"For the Pure Gifts, I was thinking of starting my homebrew attempts with the Ivory Claws. Especially since they have <i>two</i> unique Gifts: Agony and Scourging. What are you guys' thoughts about it? I was thinking of merging elements of both, since Scourging basically means &quot;to cause or experience great suffering&quot;. Also, some of the Scourging Gifts could be reskinned as rites, and some of the Agony Gifts can be folded together as Facets under the name as replacements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T13:50:15-08:00","id":747412,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:26px\"><u>Gift of Agony</u></span><br /> Werewolves who gain this Gift in any of its Facets understand its effects both when they inflict it and receive it. For the unfamiliar, pain is a crippling force, and can signal the end of their lives in an (often violent) impending death. To those who master its lessons and advantages, however, it's another tool in hunter's arsenal. <hr /><br /> <b><u>Barbed Arrow</u> [Cunning]</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Essence<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Wits + Brawl + Cunning - target's Stamina<br /> <b>Action:</b> Reflexive<br /> By using the right tool and knowing precisely where to strike, a werewolf easily cripple his quarry with minimal force. This Facet allows one to inflict considerable pain even with just a glancing blow.<br /> <br /> This Facet can be reflexively used whenever the character is performing a successful melee attack.<br /> <br /> <u>Dramatic Failure:</u><br /> <br /> <u>Failure:</u> The Facet has no effect.<br /> <br /> <u>Success:</u> On a successful attack, the Facet can inflict one of two effects. If the attack causes bashing damage, it inflicts either the Bleeding Tilt (for general attacks) or a Wrack Tilt (for called shots) if it exceeds the target's Stamina. If the attack causes lethal damage instead, it reduces the target's effective Stamina by the werewolf's Cunning Renown for the purpose of inflicting Tilts via lethal damage.<br /> <br /> <u>Exceptional Success:</u> The werewolf's ability to inflict crippling pain is magnified. The target's effective Stamina is reduced by half the werewolf's Cunning Renown (rounded up) for the purpose of inflicting Tilts via bashing damage,<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Stoicism</u> [Glory]</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Essence<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Composure + Survival + Honor<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> Through this Facet, werewolves learn to ignore their suffering. They do feel pain that is inflicted on them while this Facet is active; however, they are able to shunt that pain aside and act as fully capable warriors despite it.<br /> <br /> <u>Dramatic Failure:</u> The werewolf taps into Silver Wolf's agony, and is overwhelmed by it. He suffers from the effects of the Insane or Insensate Tilt.<br /> <br /> <u>Failure:</u> The Gift fails to take effect effect.<br /> <br /> <u>Success:</u> For the remainder of the scene, the character suffers no wound penalties, and reduces any environmental penalties affecting her by her dots in her Honor Renown.<br /> <br /> <u>Exceptional Success:</u> As success, but the effects now last for a full day.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Scourge the Impure</u> [Honor]<br /> Cost:</b> 1 Essence<br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b>Resolve + Composure + Honor<br /> <b>Action: </b>Extended (each roll represents one turn spent in a trance over the subject; the number of successes needed is the same as the Stamina + Resolve roll difficulty on p. 176 of The World of Darkness)<br /> This Facet cleanses the body of any diseases, toxins, and parasites out of a living creature (including animals, humans and Uratha), and can even exorcise most supernatural entities inhabiting mortal hosts.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Dramatic Failure:</u> The Facet rebounds on the Werewolf, who suffers the Insensate Tilt. Furthermore, he cannot use it again for the next 24 hours.<br /> <br /> <u>Failure:</u> No successes are gained for this turn.<br /> <br /> <u>Success:</u> Successes are accumulated. If enough successes are gained, the infection, disease or parasite is eliminated. Unfortunately, the Facet does not discriminate between beneficial symbiote and parasite. Most creatures' digestive tracts contain extensive quantities of microorganisms to help them digest food. The Facet eliminates those as well. This can lead to a few days of intestinal distress for the subject of the Gift, until he has eaten enough local food to re-establish the balance of his digestive systems. The target suffers from the Drugged Tilt <i>and </i>the Sick Tilt for a moderate illness for [10 - Honor Renown] Hours.<br /> <br /> If the disease or parasite is magical in nature, an additional roll is made for a Clash of Wills. Most Spirit-Ridden are considered supernatural parasites for the purpose of this Facet.<br /> <br /> <u>Exceptional Success:</u> A greater number of successes is accumulated. If five extra successes over the target are achieved on that final roll, the target's immune system does not only suffer the Facet's usual side effects, but it is supercharged for the next [Honor] days. During that time, he is treated as having the three-dot version of the Hardy Merit.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Pangs Of Anguish</u> [Purity]</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Essence<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Presence + Medicine + Purity vs. Composure + Primal Urge<br /> <b>Action:</b> Contested; resistance is reflexive<br /> With this Facet, the werewolf is able to create stabbing pain in the target. The pain usually mirrors some event in the target's life. In the case of werewolves and spirits, though, the pain mirrors that suffered by the touch of their banes (silver, in the case of Father Wolf's children). The werewolf must touch her foe in order to activate the Facet; if the target is unwilling (and he probably is), then this requires an ordinary melee attack or grapple roll. Only if the attack succeeds does the character spend Essence and make this Facet's roll.<br /> <br /> The Facet's effects lasting for a scene. If the target of the attack is an Uratha (whether Pure or Forsaken) or a spirit, any dice penalties from the pain last for a number of scenes equal to the werewolf's Primal Urge. For werewolves, the burning touch of silver is an experience that does not fade right away.<br /> <br /> <u>Dramatic Failure:</u> The Facet rebounds on the werewolf, causing him to suffer its effects as if he had scored a success.<br /> <br /> <u>Failure:</u> The target suffers no effect.<br /> <br /> <u>Success:</u> The target suffers from the Stunned Tilt, and receives a dice penalty on all actions equal to the werewolf's Purity dots for the rest of the scene (or a number of scenes equal to the werewolf's Primal Urge if the target is a spirit or another werewolf).<br /> <br /> <u>Exceptional Success:</u> The target is left reeling from the pain that he finds it hard to center himself. He gains the Disoriented Condition.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b><u>World of Pain</u> [Wisdom]</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Essence<br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b>Presence + Empathy + Wisdom<br /> By their nature, spirits do not suffer the same frailties as creatures of Flesh. They may be harmed, yes, but they do not experience pain as humans and werewolves do. An Uratha who possesses this Facet can rectify that situation, exposing any spirits within his area of influence to the hardships of the World of Flesh.<br /> <br /> <u>Dramatic Failure:</u> The Uratha's attempts to invoke the Facet backfire on him. He loses a number of Essence points equal to (6 - the number of dots away from Harmony 5), and cannot use this power again for the next 24 hours.<br /> <br /> <u>Failure:</u> The Facet produces no effect.<br /> <br /> <u>Success</u>: The Uratha exudes a protective field which grounds spirits within [10 x Wisdom] yards to the physical world for the duration of the scene. Affected spirits must make a Clash of Wills [Power + Rank vs. Wisdom + Primal Urge] whenever they enter this field. If they fail, they are forced into material form and lose a number of Essence points equal to [6 - Rank]. Any attempts to either return to ephemeral form or to escape this field necessitate another Clash of Wills.<br /> <br /> <u>Exceptional Success:</u> The spirit is anchored so forcibly into the World of Flesh that it is rattled gravely by the experience. On a failed Clash of Wills, it loses Essence equal to [11 - Rank]. Furthermore, each point of aggravated damage it suffers places a cumulative -1 penalty (up to a maximum equal to the Werewolf's Wisdom Renown), which persists until it can escape the field or the werewolf ends the effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 01-24-2016, 09:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T14:19:05-08:00","id":747449,"title":"","content":"The Fire Touched have two unique gifts too. Disease and Fervor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T14:28:01-08:00","id":747463,"title":"","content":"Ah. Well, I am open to suggestions on how to address this. Unlike Scourging, Disease actually does feel like a Shadow Gift.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T17:54:47-08:00","id":748005,"title":"","content":"Fever Gifts, as well, my personal favorite. Though non-Fire Touched and Forsaken could learn these things, they were just not usually sought after by others and would often be seen as sort of a blasphemous act, using the primary weapons of the antagonist.<br /> <br /> They've fully unlocked that now, explicitly stating anyone can get any Shadow gift, but moon gifts are still locked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T21:18:53-08:00","id":748379,"title":"","content":"Added the Wisdom Facet to my take on the Gift of Agony.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T12:39:32-08:00","id":749751,"title":"","content":"For me your Honor Facet of Agony Gifts sounds much more as Glory one - Honor ones are about &quot;making right thing to do&quot;, Glory ones are about &quot;making awesome stuff&quot;/&quot;being badass warrior&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T15:37:28-08:00","id":750224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=749751#post749751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me your Honor Facet of Agony Gifts sounds much more as Glory one - Honor ones are about &quot;making right thing to do&quot;, Glory ones are about &quot;making awesome stuff&quot;/&quot;being badass warrior&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hmm. You got a point. I might make that the Glory Facet instead and think up a new one to fill in for Honor. Any suggestions for that Facet's concept?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T18:01:57-08:00","id":750368,"title":"","content":"Finally completed my conversion of the Agony Gift with this Facet, adapted from the 1e Scourging Gift. It's still incomplete, though, since I need to work out the mechanics for supernatural illnesses and parasites. A Clash of Wills seems like a good place to start.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><u>Scourge the Impure</u> [Honor]<br /> Cost:</b> 1 Essence<br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b>Resolve + Composure + Honor<br /> <b>Action: </b>Extended (each roll represents one turn spent in a trance over the subject; the number of successes needed is the same as the Stamina + Resolve roll difficulty on p. 176 of The World of Darkness)<br /> Considered a benediction to Silver Wolf by the Ivory Claws, this Facet embodies espouses the concept that unalike things should not mix. It cleanses the body of any diseases, toxins, and parasites out of a living creature (including animals, humans and Uratha), and can even exorcise most supernatural entities inhabiting mortal hosts.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Dramatic Failure:</u> The Facet rebounds on the Werewolf, who suffers the Insensate Tilt. Furthermore, he cannot use it again for the next 24 hours.<br /> <br /> <u>Failure:</u> No successes are gained for this turn.<br /> <br /> <u>Success:</u> Successes are accumulated. If enough successes are gained, the infection, disease or parasite is eliminated. Unfortunately, the Facet does not discriminate between beneficial symbiote and parasite. Most creatures' digestive tracts contain extensive quantities of microorganisms to help them digest food. The Facet eliminates those as well. This can lead to a few days of intestinal distress for the subject of the Gift, until he has eaten enough local food to re-establish the balance of his digestive systems. The target suffers from the Drugged Tilt <i>and </i>the Sick Tilt for a moderate illness for [10 - Honor Renown] Hours.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Exceptional Success:</u> A greater number of successes is accumulated. If five extra successes over the target are achieved on that final roll, the target's immune system does not only suffer the Facet's usual side effects, but it is supercharged for the next [Honor] days. During that time, he is treated as having the three-dot version of the Hardy Merit. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T18:40:34-08:00","id":750397,"title":"","content":"What about the supernatural resistances?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T21:50:01-08:00","id":750697,"title":"","content":"Still trying to iron out the details. But so far, I was thinking something involving a Clash of Wills. The original Scourging Gift (Expel) 'did not work on magical diseases, viruses or prion-based diseases'.<br /> <br /> <b>Update:</b> Put up some specific mechanics, now. But I still need critique.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 11-03-2015, 12:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T22:18:46-08:00","id":750715,"title":"","content":"<u><span style=\"font-size:26px\">Gift of Savagery</span></u><br /> At its heart, a predator is a savage creature. And the Uratha are no exception. Those who seek to master the Gift of Savagery take this primal truth, and shape it into another tool in their hunts. Among the Pure, Predator Kings are masters at controlling their feral instincts and manipulating such savagery in others. Those with this Gift become more capable killers, and even more lethal foes in a hunt. Similarly, Blood Talons who have had the Gift marked upon their bodies are counted among the most vicious of their tribe. And more than once have they felled prey who made the mistake of underestimating their ferocity. <hr /><br /> <b><u>Challenger's Instinct</u> [Cunning]</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>1 Essence<br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b>Wits + Investigation + Cunning vs. Manipulation + Subterfuge<br /> <b>Action:</b> Reflexive<br /> The Predator King with this Facet can sense the depths of Rage boiling within another werewolf, but only when the enemy is immersed in his purest fury. Anshega with this ability use it on foes to read the telltale signs in body language, spirit brands and the aura of a fellow predator to determine how deep the hunter's fury runs in their opponent's psyche. It is a bald, open study of another hunter, often employed to locate and face down the most-skilled combatant in an enemy pack. This Facet only works on Uratha in Dalu or Gauru form that the character can see directly.<br /> <br /> <u>Dramatic Failure:</u> The werewolf completely misinterprets the target of the Facet. The werewolf learns how many turns the target can spend in Gauru form, but the number is either significantly higher or lower than the true figure.<br /> <br /> <u>Failure:</u> The werewolf is unable to sense anything about the target's Rage at all.<br /> <br /> <u>Success:</u> The werewolf perceives the target's inner fury and can tell how many turns his opponent can spend in the Gauru form before he must change back. The werewolf also learns what specific stimuli incites his foe into Kuruth.<br /> <br /> <u>Exceptional Success:</u> As a success, but the Predator King becomes deeply attuned to the target's fury, and can predict the ebb and flow of his foe's anger. In combat against the target, the character receives a bonus to his Brawl and Defense equal to his Cunning Renown as he predicts and interprets his attacker's wild, Rage-driven strikes.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Savage Feast</u> [Glory]</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Essence<br /> <b>Action:</b> Reflexive<br /> This Facet is only usable while in Gauru form. Whenever the character kills another living creature in a combat scene, he gains a series of cumulative bonuses that build with each of her slain targets. He gains +1 to both attack rolls and Defense, as well as a point of Willpower (which does not go above his maximum score). Hence, if the character kills three individuals -- be they guard dogs, mortal thugs, or other werewolves -- he now has +3 to attack rolls, +3 to his Defense, and three new points of Willpower. What is reaped, is sown. The bonuses to attack and defend max out at a score equal to his Glory Renown, however, and disappear after the character shifts to another form. The Willpower points remain, however, until spent or otherwise lost.<br /> <br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Unshackled Rage</u> [Honor]</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Essence per target<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Manipulation + Expression + Honor vs. Composure + Primal Urge<br /> <b>Action:</b> Contested; resistance is considered reflexive<br /> With this Facet, the Predator King has mastered his own savagery and anger to the point where he can fiercely project it onto others, making them experience the depths of his potential for viciousness. More than that, he can focus his anger so powerfully that it can steal the rational thoughts of humans and other werewolves, causing humans to act like savage animals, and pushing Uratha close to Kuruth.<br /> <br /> <u>Dramatic Failure:</u> The attempted projection of the character's killing urges backfires, and he must test for Death Rage.<br /> <br /> <u>Failure:</u> The Gift has no effect.<br /> <br /> <u>Success:</u> The minds of the targets are clouded in animalist fury, making people act on their most savage instincts. Each individual targeted suffers the following effects depending on their nature.<br /> <br /> Werewolves must roll for Death Rage, and treat their effective Harmony as one step lower for the purpose of resisting Death Rage stimuli for the scene.<br /> <br /> Humans become violently angry with the closest person to them (including the werewolf if appropriate). They suffer the effects of the Berserk Condition for the remainder of the scene.<br /> <br /> <u>Exceptional Success:</u> As with a success, though a werewolf affected by the Facet falls into Wasu-Im on the spot. Furthermore, the effects now last a number of scenes equal to the werewolf's Honor Renown.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Unstoppable Fury</u> [Purity]<br /> Cost:</b> 3 Essence<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> None<br /> <b>Action:</b> Reflexive<br /> Once a werewolf lets loose his savage nature, there are few things capable of stopping him. This point is made firmly clear for those who call upon this Facet. Upon invoking it, the werewolf becomes more impervious to injuries that would otherwise kill a normal human being. Each attack made during the remainder of the scene has an amount of damage equal to the werewolf's Purity Renown downgraded by one level. If the werewolf falls into Basu-Im, he can activate this Facet at no cost.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b>Predator's Presence [Wisdom]<br /> Co\u200bst:</b> 1 Essence<br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b>Presence + Intimidation + Wisdom<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> A werewolf's innate Primal Urge separates her from nearby humans. Under the effects of this Facet, people know on a subconscious level that a predator is nearby. This can make them uncomfortable and reluctant to respond favorably to a werewolf even in her human form.<br /> <br /> <u>Dramatic Failure:</u> The werewolf fails to project her predatory aura with any subtlety, instead sending subconscious threats to all nearby. The werewolf applies half her Primal Urge as a penalty to all social rolls (except Intimidation) for the duration of the scene.<br /> <br /> <u>Failure:</u> The Facet has no effect.<br /> <br /> <u>Success:</u> The werewolf masters her hunter's aura and focuses it upon nearby humans. The werewolf applies her Wisdom as social penalties to any human who interacts with her for the rest of the scene. People react to the werewolf with obedience, placidity, even a little fear until the werewolf leaves their presence.<br /> <br /> <u>Exceptional Success:</u> The werewolf further heightens her domination over the prey creatures, and any human she interacts with for a number of hours equal to her Wisdom Renown suffer the indicated social penalties while in her presence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 01-11-2016, 05:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T00:52:09-08:00","id":793010,"title":"","content":"With the details for designing 2E Gift Facets (and porting over 1E Gifts) now out, I am probably going to revisit what I've written down, so far, to see if there are any improvements needed.<br /> <br /> That said, I've made some changes to the Gift of Agony. And I might move on, now, to the Gift of Disease.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T20:06:53-08:00","id":793388,"title":"","content":"<u><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:26px\">Gift of Diseases</span></span></u><br /> Many stories about werewolves speak of how they create more of their kind by infecting their victims through their bites. Some of them may have been inspired by invocations of this particular Gift. They allow one of the People to bring to bear the crippling touch of sickness, ensuring a slow but certain death for their prey. While the Fire-Touched tend to favor these powers and their various applications, most other werewolves (Pure and Forsaken alike) tend to shun them. This is due to more than just the difficulty of containing whatever pestilence the Gift can unleash. Some stories of Father Wolf's death hint that it wasn't the claws of his children, but a poisonous bite from either the Spinner Hag or the Plague King that ultimately led to his demise. These tales, and more conventional stories from human mythology, do more than an adequate job of making poison and disease a coward's weapons. <hr /><br /> <u><b>Wasting Sickness</b></u><b> [Cunning]</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3 Essence<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Manipulation + Medicine + Cunning<br /> <b>Action:</b> Extended; 10 successes required (Each roll represents 1 minute)<br /> <br /> This Facet enables a werewolf to infect a target with a slow disease. The target sickens over a period of days, and, unless treated quickly and expertly, dies in less than week. Wasting Sickness can even be fatal to Uratha, though with their regenerative powers they are usually able to shake it off before death occurs. While the disease is not normally contagious, some werewolves of exceptional power have been able to unleash supernatural epidemics given enough time and energy.<br /> <br /> <u>Dramatic Failure:</u> The Fire-Touched contracts the non-transmittable version of the disease, and suffers the effects of the Facet.<br /> <br /> <u>Failure:</u> No successes are accumulated.<br /> <br /> <u>Success:</u> Progress is made toward the goal. Once the target number is reached, the werewolf becomes a carrier for the disease. The next person he bites becomes infected with the disease. Human beings cannot resist infection; they can only try to stave off the effects. Supernatural victims can resist with a Clash of Wills. Regardless, all infected suffer lethal damage equal to the werewolf's Cunning Renown per day. A victim may resist this damage by rolling Stamina + Resolve.<br /> <br /> Damage from the disease can be overcome normally (which is why werewolves seldom die from it), but the modifier persists for as long as the disease does. Fighting off the disease requires an extended Stamina + Resolve roll. Uratha characters need 10 successes to fight off the disease, while humans require 20. One roll can be made per day, but the -3 modifier applies to this roll. If the character is under the care of a doctor or healer, successes from Intelligence + Medicine rolls (again, one roll per day) can be added to the total.<br /> <br /> <u>Exceptional Success:</u> If the werewolf reaches 15+ successes on the final roll, he can opt to make the disease contagious. If so, it spreads like the common cold. Casual contact allows a Stamina + Resolve roll to avoid infection, but intimate contact (include prolonged physical contact, sex or a bite) means automatic infection for humans.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Glorious Malady</u> [Glory]</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Essence<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Stamina + Survival + Glory<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <br /> By activating this Facet, the werewolf taints his own Essence with a spiritual malady. This illness actually makes the werewolf stronger and deadlier, lending the pain of disease and contagion to his claws and fangs. The werewolf must sacrifice his own regenerative powers to allow the disease to run its course, however, and many have perished under the effects. Once activated, Glorious Malady lasts for the scene, unless it is terminated early with the expenditure of an Essence point.<br /> <br /> <u>Dramatic Failure:</u> The werewolf loses his regeneration for the scene, but gains no benefit. He suffers from the grave version of the Sick Tilt.<br /> <br /> <u>Failure:</u> The Facet has no effects.<br /> <br /> <u>Success:</u> The werewolf experiences a rush of adrenaline, and tastes bile oozing from his gums. The disease grants a bonus equal to his Glory Renown to all Strength- or Stamina-based rolls for the remainder of the scene. In addition, his bite and claw attacks have a chance of inflicting the Sick Tilt due to the caustic sludge from the werewolf's mouth and fingernails. For the rest of the scene, however, the werewolf does not regenerate, cannot spend Essence to heal lethal damage, and takes a point of bashing per turn in combat.<br /> <br /> <u>Exceptional Success:</u> The werewolf's regeneration returns after [6 - Glory] turns. Additionally, his attacks inflict the grave version of the Sick Tilt.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b>Stroke of Madness [Honor]<br /> Cost:</b> 3 Essence<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Presence + Intimidation + Honor vs. Resolve + Primal Urge<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <br /> Diseases can not only plague the body. They can also scar the mind, itself. By invoking this Facet as he stares down his prey, the werewolf inflicts a sense of extreme delirium and vertigo which can drive all but the strong-willed to the brink of insanity.<br /> <br /> <u>Dramatic Failure:</u> The Facet not only fails to take effect, but the Essence used to invoke it rebounds on the werewolf. He suffers from the Soul Shocked Condition, and cannot use this power again for the remainder of the scene.<br /> <br /> <u>Failure:</u> The Facet fails to take effect.<br /> <br /> <u>Success:</u> The target's mind snaps under the sheer force of the werewolf's force of will. He suffers from either the Insane or Insensate Tilt for a number of turns equal to the werewolf's Honor Renown.<br /> <br /> <u>Exceptional Success:</u> The delirium imposed by the Facet is so overpowering that the victim's will is thoroughly ravaged. In addition to the above effects, he gains the Soul Shocked Condition.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Plague Bearer</u> [Purity]</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Essence<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Wits + Occult + Purity<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <br /> Perhaps the most blatant Facet to the Gift of Diseases, a werewolf who bears it can exhale a cloud of toxins and diseases. Any who come into contact with it without any form of protection and/or cannot fight off its effects will only watch in horror as buboes, necrotic cysts and pox marks erupt on their skin.<br /> <br /> <u>Dramatic Failure:</u> The werewolf finds himself infected with the very toxins he sought to let loose. He immediately takes a point of aggravated damage, and must roll to resist falling into Basu-Im.<br /> <br /> <u>Failure:</u> The Facet has no effect; the werewolf does not breathe out anything.<br /> <br /> <u>Success:</u> The werewolf breathes out a thick cloud of miasma with a diameter in yards equal to twice his Purity Renown. This cloud lasts for a number of turns equal to the successes rolled (the effects end earlier, though, should the cloud be dissipated). Anyone caught within the cloud must roll Stamina + Resolve for every turn they are enveloped. On a failure, they suffer the grave version of the Poisoned Tilt.<br /> <br /> <u>Exceptional Success:</u> The various diseases which comprise the miasma can induce additional side-effects upon their victims. In addition to the above effects, the cloud also inflicts the Drugged Tilt.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Fever Dreams</u> [Wisdom]<br /> Cost: </b>1 Essence<br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b>Presence + Medicine + Wisdom vs. Resolve + Primal Urge<br /> <b>Action: </b>Reflexive<br /> <br /> The werewolf passes along a spiritual infection to a target. Although this disease runs its course quickly, and rarely does any serious damage to the target, it causes the victim to suffers cold sweats, headaches, fever and even mild hallucinations. Needless to say, fighting or even focusing his mind is extremely difficult while the disease holds him. This Facet can only be activated with a successful touch action.<br /> <br /> <u>Dramatic Failure:</u> The werewolf suffers from the Sick Tilt for the remainder of the scene.<br /> <br /> <u>Failure:</u> The Facet fails to take effect, and the infection therefore does not take root.<br /> <br /> <u>Success:</u> The subject suffers as described above. For a number of turns equal to the successes rolled, the victim suffers from the Disoriented Condition.<br /> <br /> <u>Exceptional Success:</u> The disease takes an even greater toll on the victim's body. In addition to the effects of a success, he also suffers both the Stunned Tilt and lethal damage equal to the werewolf's Wisdom Renown.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 12-28-2015, 10:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T09:06:53-08:00","id":793605,"title":"","content":"Yay Pure gifts!<br /> <br /> Questions and comments.<br /> <br /> Agony: Barbed Arrow - Mechanically this could be a nightmare. Stamina can't be reduced past 1 or can it? If it does it is to powerful, if it doesn't it still reduces over all health then? Even slaughterer would be a bit underpowered compared to this.<br /> <br /> Savagery: Savage Might - I would recommend either one or the other, having a static bonus to a trait and gaining the 8 again quality is a bit much. for instance, Rahu gain the 8 again quality with brawl or weaponry, and anyone with primal strength can get that nice purity bonus, but both seems a bit overpowered.<br /> <br /> Savagery: Unending Fury - Realistically, this will not work out. It is far easier to take easier triggers, or take a certain merit to fall into Basu-im. The amount of aggravated damage taken, the time needed to recover, it just isn't worth it as a facet.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, I love all the gifts!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8177-heroofthemists","name":"Heroofthemists","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T14:53:18-08:00","id":793794,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure Predator Kings already get Strength as affinity, so you might want to avoid any facets too similar to what that provides.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T15:23:25-08:00","id":793805,"title":"","content":"Maybe something like Harvest of Glorious Fury for the Glory Facet on Savagery?<br /> <br /> Like:<br /> <br /> <b>Harvest of Glorious Fury</b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost:</span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 1 Essence</span> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Action:</span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Reflexive</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">While in Gauru form, any time the character kills another living creature he gains a series of cumulative bonuses that build with each of her slain targets. He gains: (A) +1 to attack rolls. (B) One point of Willpower (though not past the character's maximum pool). (C) +1 to Defense. So, if the character kills three individuals -- be they guard dogs, mortal thugs, or other werewolves -- he now has +3 to attack rolls, +3 to his Defense, and three new points of Willpower. What is reaped, is sown. The bonuses to attack and defend disappear after the character leaves Garou. The Willpower points remain, however, until spent or otherwise lost.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T16:16:13-08:00","id":793826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heroofthemists</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=793605#post793605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yay Pure gifts!<br /> <br /> Questions and comments.<br /> <br /> Agony: Barbed Arrow - Mechanically this could be a nightmare. Stamina can't be reduced past 1 or can it? If it does it is to powerful, if it doesn't it still reduces over all health then? Even slaughterer would be a bit underpowered compared to this.<br /> <br /> Savagery: Savage Might - I would recommend either one or the other, having a static bonus to a trait and gaining the 8 again quality is a bit much. for instance, Rahu gain the 8 again quality with brawl or weaponry, and anyone with primal strength can get that nice purity bonus, but both seems a bit overpowered.<br /> <br /> Savagery: Unending Fury - Realistically, this will not work out. It is far easier to take easier triggers, or take a certain merit to fall into Basu-im. The amount of aggravated damage taken, the time needed to recover, it just isn't worth it as a facet.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, I love all the gifts!</div> </div> </div> </div>Barbed Arrow - I should probably have included &quot;down to a minimum rating of 1&quot;, with regards to that. Thanks for pointing it out, Though I do have to stress that it's just reducing the effective Stamina for the purpose of inflicting Tilts. Think of it like a 'watered down' version of the Gauru form's ability to inflict Tilts in battle.<br /> <br /> Unending Fury - I am open to suggestions for revising/replacing this Facet.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=793794#post793794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure Predator Kings already get Strength as affinity, so you might want to avoid any facets too similar to what that provides.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. That's the challenging part besides working out the mechanics of the Facets.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=793805#post793805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Harvest of Glorious Fury</b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost:</span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 1 Essence</span> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Action:</span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Reflexive</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">While in Gauru form, any time the character kills another living creature he gains a series of cumulative bonuses that build with each of her slain targets. He gains: (A) +1 to attack rolls. (B) One point of Willpower (though not past the character's maximum pool). (C) +1 to Defense. So, if the character kills three individuals -- be they guard dogs, mortal thugs, or other werewolves -- he now has +3 to attack rolls, +3 to his Defense, and three new points of Willpower. What is reaped, is sown. The bonuses to attack and defend disappear after the character leaves Garou. The Willpower points remain, however, until spent or otherwise lost.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. Interesting. But just to clarify, though, is this an existing Facet? Or is it original?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 12-27-2015, 07:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T16:32:19-08:00","id":793834,"title":"","content":"Not original. It was a gift in 1e that has no 2e equivalent.<br /> <br /> I believe it was a Glory gift (so Cahalith only) but it seems very appropriate for a Savagery Facet. I had it copy/pasted in one of my files.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T16:45:07-08:00","id":793841,"title":"","content":"It certainly is. Yeah, I think I can slot this in as a Savagery Facet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T16:46:49-08:00","id":793843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <u><b>S</b></u><b><u>avage Might</u> [Glory]</b><br /> Werewolves who bear this Facet are often feared by their packmates for the unbridled might they display in battle. None can deny, though, the incredible killing Rage that pulses in their bones and allows them to tear their enemies apart. The Werewolf gains a bonus equal to her Glory Renown and the 8-again on all Strength-based dice pools while in Gauru Form. However, when all her health boxes are filled with lethal damage, she immediately slips into Wasu-Im. </div> </div> </div>Replaced this with &quot;Savage Harvest&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T04:11:02-08:00","id":794079,"title":"","content":"Finished my conversion of Disease. Took a look at the 1E Fever Gift for inspiration on some of the Facets. Again, critique is appreciated.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=750715#post750715\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=750715#post750715\"> Werewolf Gifts - 2e Conversion - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=750715#post750715\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=750715#post750715 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Seeing as Werewolf 2e players have a shortage of official Moon Gifts as well as Gifts tied to the Pure, I'm putting up this thread for those interested in </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T07:39:10-08:00","id":794178,"title":"","content":"Moving away from the Pure Gifts, now, to try my hand at converting 1E Auspice Gifts into 2E Moon Gifts. My first attempt will be on converting the Stalker's Moon Gifts. Any suggestions and ideas will be welcome. Right now, I am debating what to put in place of See Heat (the two-dot power) and Liar's Brand (the three-dot power). The former is already covered by the Gift of Hunting's Wisdom Facet, and the latter doesn't seem to fit well with the 2E rules. There's also the matter of making the three-dot power be something tied to the Siskur-Dah Condition, according to the guide for designing/converting Moon Gifts.<br /> <br /> I also have an alternative name suggested for the converted Stalker's Moon: &quot;Gift of the Shadow Moon&quot;. Do I go with that or stick with the original name?<br /> <br /> <u><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:26px\">Gift of the Stalker's Moon</span></span></u> <hr /><b><u>Soundless Strike</u> (o)</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Essence<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Dexterity + Stealth + Cunning<br /> <b>Action:</b> Reflexive<br /> <br /> Using this Facet, the Irraka can strike in a single moment of blessed silence. Claws tear through flesh without a sound, a victim's mouth strains to form a scream that will not come. Though the moment of silence is fleeting, a cunning Irraka can turn it into a great opportunity. This Gift must be invoked during the Irraka's turn.<br /> <br /> <u>Dramatic Failure:</u> The Gift fails, and the Irraka is rattled by its failure. The Irraka suffers a -1 penalty to the action in question.<br /> <br /> <u>Failure:</u> The Gift has no effect.<br /> <br /> <u>Success:</u> The Irraka's attack happens in complete silence. If he tears the leg off a victim, the victim's scream is without sound. If he fires a gun at point-blank range, the report is inaudible.<br /> <br /> <u>Exceptional Success:</u> If the Irraka's target survives, her next turn is also spent in complete silence, preventing her from crying for help.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b>(oo)</b><br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b>(ooo)</b><br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Stolen Scent</u> (oooo)</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Essence<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Manipulation + Survival + Cunning<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <br /> It's one thing to leave no scent. It's quite another to leave a misleading one. The Irraka with this Facet can alter his scent however he likes, even going so far as leaving the scent of a rival at the scene of a murder. Given how many werewolves trust their noses before their eyes, this is no small thing.<br /> <br /> <u>Dramatic Failure:</u> The Irraka only enhances his own scent, smelling more pungent than usual for the duration of the scene.<br /> <br /> <u>Failure:</u> The Gift fails to work.<br /> <br /> <u>Success:</u> The Irraka leaves the scent of the target of his choice behind wherever he walks. He may duplicate any scent he is familiar with (that is to say, any scent he's reliably observed in Urshul or Urhan form) -- human or animal, of any gender, even mimicking the scent of a wounded or sick creature. He may change his scent as many times as he likes while the Gift remains in effect. This Facet lasts for one hour per success, although the Irraka may cancel its effects at any time as a reflexive action.<br /> <br /> <u>Exceptional Success:</u> No additional effect.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Strike Blind</u> (ooooo)</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 2 Essence<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Wits + Medicine + Cunning vs. target's Composure + Primal Urge<br /> <b>Action:</b> Contested; resistance is reflexive<br /> <br /> The Irraka strives to deceive the senses of others, but isn't above removing them entirely. This Facet enables the Irraka to strike a foe blind, to make her go deaf or to rob her of her sense of smell. Any one of the three is a terrible punishment for a werewolf, but human prey are particularly vulnerable to losing their sight.<br /> <br /> <u>Dramatic Failure:</u> The Irraka catches a bit of backlash from the Gift. For the rest of the scene, the Irraka suffers a -1 penalty to all perception-related rolls.<br /> <br /> <u>Failure:</u> The Gift fails to work.<br /> <br /> <u>Success:</u> The victim is struck blind, deaf or scentblind; the Irraka chooses which sense is affected. The sensory loss lasts for a number of hours equal to the werewolf's Cunning Renown.<br /> <br /> <u>Exceptional Success:</u> The sensory loss lasts for a number of days equal to the werewolf's Cunning Renown.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 12-28-2015, 08:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T07:31:01-08:00","id":804440,"title":"","content":"My first thought is to ask what you intend the theme of your 2e Stalker's Moon gift to be? What is the 'stalker' you want here?<br /> <br /> Second thoughts are:<br /> - Soundless Strike seems reasonable.<br /> - Stolen Scent seems too narrow, mainly because of it just being scent.<br /> - Strike Blind seems underwhelming for a capstone, even though it is a solid effect.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T09:01:55-08:00","id":804490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=804440#post804440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My first thought is to ask what you intend the theme of your 2e Stalker's Moon gift to be? What is the 'stalker' you want here?<br /> <br /> Second thoughts are:<br /> - Soundless Strike seems reasonable.<br /> - Stolen Scent seems too narrow, mainly because of it just being scent.<br /> - Strike Blind seems underwhelming for a capstone, even though it is a solid effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was going for the idea of Irraka as the hidden hunter and/or silent killer. Hence, I was thinking of renaming it as the &quot;Gift of the Shadow Moon&quot;.<br /> <br /> Moving onto your thoughts for the Facets. I may actually strike Stolen Scent off as a Facet. But perhaps keep Strike Blind after making some adjustments. Any suggestions for that, though? Also, I was thinking of porting in the two-dot power from 1E's Cunning Gift for this list. But it might overlap with the three-dot Facet of the 2E New Moon Gift. Alternatively, I was thinking of using Distractions from the 1E New Moon Gift. What do you think?<br /> <br /> <b><u>Cracks in the Armor</u> (oo)</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Essence<br /> <b>Action:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Duration:</b> One Scene<br /> An Irraka has to be ready to take advantage of any weakness and, to do that, she first needs to be able to find those hidden vulnerabilities. Upon activating this Gift, the New Moon's player adds the character's dots in the Cunning Renown as bonus dice on any roll to discern flaws, weaknesses, or other shortcomings in a person, organization, structure, item, or any other thing.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Distractions</u> (oo)<br /> Dice Pool:</b> Manipulation + Subterfuge + Cunning vs. Resolve + Primal Urge<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Duration:</b> One Scene<br /> As the werewolf spits out whispering yips and hisses, half-perceived visions much like the Irralunim themselves flit in and out of a chosen subject's range of perception, distracting him.<br /> <br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The Facet rebounds on the werewolf, assailing him with the illusions he sought to inflict on his prey. He suffers from the Disoriented Condition.<br /> <br /> <b>Failure:</b> The victim is unaffected by the visions of the Facet.<br /> <br /> <b>Success:</b> The victim is distracted by the Irraka's illusion, incurring a dice penalty on all actions equal to the werewolf's Cunning Renown.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> As a success, but the victim continues to be haunted by the visions that assailed him. He suffers from the Shadow Paranoia Condition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 01-09-2016, 12:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T09:38:55-08:00","id":804506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=804490#post804490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was going for the idea of Irraka as the hidden hunter and/or silent killer. Hence, I was thinking of renaming it as the &quot;Gift of the Shadow Moon&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's a tricky one; the core New Moon gift already covers a fair bit of hidden hunter / silent killer stuff, as does Stealth and Evasion. In that framework, I'm uncertain about Soundless Strike; a stealth-killing-focused Irraka is already going to have a high Stealth rating for pulling of silent kills as is, so its main advantage is that it absolutely silences the victim, and I'm not sure if that's really matching up to Eviscerate when it comes to establishing the feel of the Auspice from the first dot. Now the other minor advantage Soundless Strike has is that it also allows silenced gunfire but werewolf Gifts should generally veer away from firearms unless there's a really good reason, and I'm not sure this Gift has enough of a basis to break that guideline.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Moving onto your thoughts for the Facets. I may actually strike Stolen Scent off as a Facet. But perhaps keep Strike Blind after making some adjustments. Any suggestions for that, though? </div> </div> </div> My initial thoughts would be to simply make it let the Irraka inflict the Blinded or Deafened tilts with any of her melee attacks for the scene as an extra (making the Urshul free tilt particularly nasty if combo'd to do the straight-up both-eyes-Blinded effect right off. However, I then realised this largely just makes it a weak version of Butchery.<br /> <br /> I think what I'd do is probably store the idea of 'sense-based denial' in a list of useful mechanical concepts for the Gift, then delete Strike Blind entirely and start again, looking at the Gift holistically. Strike Blind by itself isn't a strong enough concept to be worth including off its own virtues; whatever goes in needs to make sense within the overall Gift concept and you can probably do better than Strike Blind as a result.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><u>Cracks in the Armor</u> (oo)</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Essence<br /> <b>Action:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Duration:</b> One Scene<br /> An Irraka has to be ready to take advantage of any weakness and, to do that, she first needs to be able to find those hidden vulnerabilities. Upon activating this Gift, the New Moon's player adds the character's dots in the Cunning Renown as bonus dice on any roll to discern flaws, weaknesses, or other shortcomings in a person, organization, structure, item, or any other thing. </div> </div> </div> Too much overlap with Prey on Weakness and possibly other Facets like Rending Claws too, depending on what discerning flaws and weaknesses in structures and items involves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><u>Distractions</u> (oo)<br /> Dice Pool:</b> Manipulation + Subterfuge + Cunning vs. Resolve + Primal Urge<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Duration:</b> One Scene<br /> As the werewolf spits out whispering yips and hisses, half-perceived visions much like the Irralunim themselves flit in and out of a chosen subject's range of perception, distracting him.<br /> <br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The Facet rebounds on the werewolf, assailing him with the illusions he sought to inflict on his prey. He suffers from the Disoriented Condition.<br /> <br /> <b>Failure:</b> The victim is unaffected by the visions of the Facet.<br /> <br /> <b>Success:</b> The victim is distracted by the Irraka's illusion, incurring a dice penalty on all actions equal to the werewolf's Cunning Renown.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> As a success, but the victim continues to be haunted by the visions that assailed him. He suffers from the Shadow Paranoia Condition. </div> </div> </div> - Cunning Renown on ALL actions for an entire scene is probably far too strong. It also overlaps a bit much conceptually with things like Divide and Conquer, Hit &amp; Run etc, which all use the general concept of distractions and disorientation to achieve specific mechanically-backed effects, whereas Distractions is vague but all-encompassing.<br /> <br /> <br /> Sorry not to have been more positive in my criticisms! You've just picked a tough one <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T09:47:03-08:00","id":804510,"title":"","content":"Well, like Chris said, it'd help to sort of decide what the Gift is really trying to accomplish. &quot;Another set of general Irraka Facets&quot; means it wouldn't offer a distinct reason for its existence, and instead just be a coin flip choice where one or the other is purchased to start with, and the other pretty soon after.<br /> <br /> So maybe consider some of the New Moon Aspects. The Scout, the Assassin, the Thief and the Fool. The latter two especially cover areas not specifically addressed by the New Moon's Gift. In which case you could maybe make The Thief's Moon or Liar's Moon. That could focus on Deception as opposed to stealth, and sowing chaos through exploiting weakness.<br /> <br /> Deep Pockets. Basically the ability to hide items untraceably. Even in plain sight? Something like the second dot of Obfuscate and the 1e Gift Deep Pockets.<br /> <br /> Stolen Visage<br /> Something that makes the Irraka switch appearances, scent, etc. with someone else (unbeknownst to the victim?). Might be too close to Stolen Skin. Doesn't require killing, maybe just touching while the victim is asleep or something.<br /> <br /> Cracks in the Armor. Basically what you have up there. Only on Siskur Dah. Maybe also add Cunning to rolls to exploit said weaknesses but the circumstances already seem a little vague. Also maybe a Subterfuge bonus here or somewhere else. This is the auspice skill that gets neglected the most for these guys.<br /> <br /> No idea. Something like Liar's Brand, maybe? That one has limited usage so I'm not sure. Maybe swap with Stolen Visage in placement.<br /> <br /> Fifth dot no idea. Something to do with Strike Blind? No damage, just robbing senses somehow. Maybe.<br /> <br /> Just some ideas. You could go with the infiltration thing, but you'd really have to double down to offer something unique, since the New Moon gift offers a few options for that already.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: Maybe throw Distractions in somewhere, but let it inflict the penalty on Mental rolls. Maybe inflict some minor illusions instead of some mechanical penalty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","user":"Amravanti","date":". 01-09-2016, 01:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T09:57:12-08:00","id":804514,"title":"","content":"This actually helps. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> At the very least, that gives me an idea on a possible name: Gift of the Lying Moon","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T10:29:06-08:00","id":804531,"title":"","content":"Glad I could help!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T11:21:43-08:00","id":804568,"title":"","content":"Okay. Second attempt at making a Moon GIft for the Irraka. This one is a power set I feel more confident about. <hr /><span style=\"font-size:26px\"><b><u>Gift of the Lying Moon</u></b></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Deep Pockets</u> (o)<br /> Cost:</b> 1 Essence<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Dexterity + Larceny + Cunning<br /> <b>Duration:</b> 1 Scene<br /> Part of the creed of Cunning is the ability to conceal what must remain hidden, even from the most intense scrutiny. An Irraka with this Facet finds his feats of legerdemain becoming more than mere parlor tricks.<br /> <br /> <u>Dramatic Failure:</u> The Facet fails to activate, instead hampering his ability to hide things by mundane means. He loses the 10-again rule on all Larceny rolls for the scene, and treats any Failures as Dramatic Failures.<br /> <br /> <u>Failure:</u> The Facet fails to take effect.<br /> <br /> <u>Success:</u> The Irraka can hide an inanimate object upon her person or within her immediate vicinity up to a Size rating equal to her Cunning Renown. Observers must succeed at a reflexive Wits + Composure with a target number equal to the werewolf's successes. Supernatural powers, meanwhile, can uncover the hidden item with a successful Clash of Wills.<br /> <br /> <u>Exceptional Success:</u> As a success, but all supernatural powers used to uncover the item suffer a -3 penalty to the Clash of Wills.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Cracks in the Armor</u></b><b> (oo)</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Essence<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Duration:</b> 1 scene<br /> The Irraka is a preternatural actor and trickster, deft of hand and sleight of tongue. And she can slip through any openings of her prey without them ever noticing. She adds her Cunning Renown on all mundane Larceny and Subterfuge rolls, and needs only three successes to achieve an exceptional success.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Elusive Hunter</u> (ooo)</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Essence<br /> <b>Action: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Duration:</b> The full duration of Siskur-Dah<br /> In the Sacred Hunt, an Irraka has to be ready to take advantage of any weaknesses presented. This Facet can only be activated when the Irraka gains the Siskur-Dah Condition. Once it's active, she adds her dots in Cunning Renown as bonus dice on any roll to discern flaws, weaknesses, or other shortcomings in a person, organization, structure, item, or any other thing.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Distractions</u> (oooo)<br /> Cost</b>: 1 Essence<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Manipulation + Subterfuge + Cunning vs. Resolve + Primal Urge<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Duration:</b> 1 Turn per Success<br /> As the werewolf spits out whispering yips and hisses, half-perceived flit in and out of a chosen subject's range of perception, hampering his ability to concentrate.<br /> <br /> <u>Dramatic Failure:</u> The Facet rebounds on the werewolf, assailing him with the illusions he sought to inflict on his prey. He suffers from the Disoriented Condition.<br /> <br /> <u>Failure:</u> The victim is unaffected by the visions of the Facet.<br /> <br /> <u>Success:</u> The victim is distracted by the Irraka's illusions, gaining the Distracted Condition for the duration of the Facet.<br /> <br /> <u>Exceptional Success:</u> As a success, but the victim is left particularly haunted by the visions. He also suffers from the Shadow Paranoia Condition.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Lying Wolfheart</u> (ooooo)<br /> Cost:</b> 3 Essence<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Manipulation + Subterfuge + Cunning<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Duration:</b> 1 Hour per Success<br /> <br /> <u>Dramatic Failure:</u> The Irraka unintentionally enhances the elusive scent of his Primal Urge. The effects of Sheep's Clothing do not apply in Hishu Form for the duration of the scene.<br /> <br /> <u>Failure:</u> The Facet fails to take effect.<br /> <br /> <u>Success:</u> For the duration of the Facet, all attempts to locate the werewolf while Sheep's Clothing is applied lose the 10-again rule, and treat any Failures as Dramatic Failures.<br /> <br /> <u>Exceptional Success:</u> Even outside the safety of the herd, it is still a challenge to hunt him down while he is in human form. Apply the normal effect of Sheep's Clothing even in sparsely populated areas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 03-07-2017, 08:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T00:00:00-08:00","id":805059,"title":"","content":"Here's another Shadow Gift conversion, largely from the Information Gift. <hr /><u><span style=\"font-size:26px\"><b>Gift of the Word</b></span></u><br /> <br /> <b><u>Twisted Words</u> [Cunning]<br /> Cost:</b> 3 Essence<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Wits + Persuasion + Cunning - Composure<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Duration:</b> 1 Scene<br /> All too often, people hear what they want to hear. A speech on a controversial subject such as immigration has the potential to warp in listener's minds until they hear what they expected or wanted to hear. This Facet goes further than that.<br /> <br /> <u>Dramatic Failure:</u> Everyone who would have been affected by the Gift hears exactly what the speaker says and nothing more, and knows that the werewolf is trying to pull the wool over her eyes.<br /> <br /> <u>Failure:</u> The character can't alter anyone's perceptions of what is said.<br /> <br /> <u>Success:</u> The werewolf can deliberately warp one group's perceptions of the speech in a direction of her choosing. Listeners can make a reflexive Resolve + Persuasion roll to attempt to follow what sounds like a lunatic screed or untangle a speech's distorted meaning. The selection can be a wide group, but the Facet has no effect beyond a radius equal to [Cunning x5] yards.<br /> <br /> <u>Exceptional Success:</u> As success, but none of the listeners may make a Resolve + Persuasion roll to determine the original meaning of the speech.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Babel</u> [Glory]<br /> Cost:</b> 3 Essence<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Manipulation + Persuasion + Glory vs. Composure + Primal Urge<br /> <b>Action:</b> Contested; resistance is reflexive<br /> <b>Duration:</b> 1 Scene<br /> Language is a means of conveying structured information, a means of spreading ideas from one person to another. Language is a remarkably versatile form, and even a mild grasp of a tongue will allow someone to convey a wide range of basic ideas. This Facet shatters that by crudely reorganizing the information that underlies a conversation. Those targeted by this power appear to see every other member of their group suffering from dysphasia.<br /> <br /> <u>Dramatic Failure:</u> The werewolf is unable to make herself understood to anyone using anything more complex than crude physical gestures for the rest of the scene.<br /> <br /> <u>Failure:</u> The targets of the Facet remain able to understand one another.<br /> <br /> <u>Success:</u> The werewolf targets members of an identifiable group (gang members, or a hunting party) within a radius of [Glory x5] yards. Each target must make a contested roll. Those who fail are entirely unable to communicate with the others using any form of organized language -- including sign language -- and must rely on crude gestures to convey any meaning. While any member of the group who is not affected can be understood by those who are, those affected cannot make themselves understood to anyone else in the group. This effectively ruins the group's co-ordination, making most tactics effectively impossible. The result of this is that each affected member suffers a -3 modifier to all rolls where communication with the other affected people is a factor, and treat all Failures as Dramatic Failures.<br /> <br /> <u>Exceptional Success:</u> The werewolf poisons the underpinnings of his targets' communication. Anyone suffering this level of effect cannot make himself understood by anyone, as opposed to just members of the same group.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Tongues</u> [Honor]<br /> Cost:</b> 1 Essence<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Honor Hours<br /> Humanity has hundreds of languages in use today, and hundreds more that have seen use during past centuries. This Facet allows the werewolf to speak and understand the language of any human he is speaking with, whether it is face-to-face or over the phone, as long as he can hear the subject's voice. Furthermore, the Facet allows the werewolf to understand something written in a foreign language without knowing the language in question.<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Wits + Academics + Honor<br /> <br /> <u>Dramatic Failure:</u> The translation is botched, appearing to convey the basic meaning of the text but with enough alterations to dramatically alter the actual meaning of the piece. All rolls relating to the translated information have a -1 modifier.<br /> <br /> <u>Failure:</u> The Facet does not grant any insights into the text.<br /> <br /> <u>Success:</u> The Facet allows the Werewolf to divine the literal meaning of the text.<br /> <br /> <u>Exceptional Success:</u> The Facet effortlessly translates not only the text but also the deeper subtext and other subtleties concealed in the words.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Speak the Words</u> [Purity]<br /> Cost:</b> 1 Essence<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Presence + Expression + Purity<br /> <b>Action: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Purity Hours<br /> It is said in some tales that the <i>Uremehir </i>was the first language ever spoken by humans. While the herd demonstrate little to no understanding of the First Tongue, a werewolf can impart momentary insight to an individual of his choice.<br /> <br /> <u>Dramatic Failure:</u> Rather than give him the ability to speak a lost language, the target of the Facet loses any ability to speak at all. He gain the Mute Condition for the scene.<br /> <br /> <u>Failure:</u> The Facet fails to impart its effect on the target.<br /> <br /> <u>Success:</u> For the duration of the Facet, anyone targeted by it can understand a spirit communicating with him in the First Tongue. He may not be able to respond in kind, but it does give him some idea of the entity's current disposition.<br /> <br /> <u>Exceptional Success:</u> As success, but the target can now speak the words of the First Tongue until the end of the Facet's duration.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Fine Print</u> [Wisdom]<br /> Cost:</b> 1 Essence per target recipient<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Intelligence + Subterfuge + Cunning<br /> <b>Action:</b> Extended (10 successes; 10 minutes pass per roll)<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Special (See Below)<br /> Language is a carrier for information, a means of encoding thought and meaning -- information -- in to another person. This Facet allows the werewolf to add hidden information to her words, encoding a message or meaning that only someone of her choosing will understand. Anyone else reading or hearing her words will hear what she says, but her chosen recipient will also understand a message just for him.<br /> <br /> <u>Dramatic Failure:</u> The werewolf's message is either warped as it is hidden so that it has a different meaning, or someone other than the desired target receives the hidden message.<br /> <br /> <u>Failure:</u> The message conveys no extra meaning.<br /> <br /> <u>Success:</u> The werewolf hides a message underneath what she is saying. Any individual she can identify, or members of a distinct group, will hear both messages, though the werewolf must spend one Essence per recipient. If there aren't enough people present, the extra Essence is wasted. If there are more present, the Storyteller decides who hears the message and who does not. The hidden message cannot be longer than the original message.<br /> <br /> <u>Exceptional Success:</u> As a success, but all members of a group hear the message for only one Essence. Any extra Essence spent is returned to the werewolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 04-15-2018, 06:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T04:37:18-08:00","id":805146,"title":"","content":"Revised the Purity Facet for the Gift of Savagery.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=750715#post750715\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=750715#post750715\"> Werewolf Gifts - 2e Conversion - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=750715#post750715\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=750715#post750715 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Seeing as Werewolf 2e players have a shortage of official Moon Gifts as well as Gifts tied to the Pure, I'm putting up this thread for those interested in </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Here's the previous version for those curious:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><u>Unending Fury</u> [Purity]</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Essence<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> None<br /> <b>Action:</b> Action<br /> To fall into Kuruth is to abandon all reason for the purest instinct of all -- to survive at any cost. Some Predator Kings have learned not to fear the touch of Death Rage, but to welcome it as the epitome of the hunter's arsenal against his prey. This Gift suppresses the hunter's fight or flight instincts, so that they do not feel the instinctive urge to preserve their life when nearing death. Instead, they lose themselves to mindless Rage, ripping flesh and lashing out with no desire beyond killing their enemies. Predator Kings who are blinded by hate for the enemies, who simply wish to take down as many of their foes as possible before their own death or who are certain victory can come with a final-breath effort, use this Facet with devastating effects.<br /> <br /> Upon activating this Facet, the Werewolf falls into Basu-Im, and adds his Purity Renown to his effective Primal Urge for determining its duration (at Storyteller discretion, this can go beyond Primal Urge 10). While active, any attack that would inflict bashing damage on the werewolf inflicts only a single point, and all lethal and aggravated damage is downgraded by one level. In addition, all wound penalties he suffers are converted into bonuses.<br /> <br /> This ability comes at a steep price, however. If the Werewolf has survived long enough to emerge from Basu-Im, he suffers aggravated damage to all of his health boxes. Successes on a Stamina + Primal Urge roll downgrades a fraction of that damage to lethal on a 1-to-1 basis. Completely surrendering to the Rage and embracing the raw power it brings is a fatal experience for all but the hardiest of Uratha.<br /> <br /> If the character is down to his last three health boxes, he may activate this reflexively at no cost. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T06:05:34-08:00","id":806016,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><u>Gift of Fervor</u></span></b><br /> <br /> <b><u>Lapse of Faith</u> [Cunning]<br /> Cost:</b> 1 Essence<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Presence + Expression + Cunning vs. Resolve + Primal Urge<br /> <b>Action:</b> Reflexive and Contested<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Scene<br /> The werewolf can force a spiritual compulsion that hinders her prey's attempts at fighting back against him. It can potentially even force him to turn on those he's fighting alongside.<br /> <br /> <u>Dramatic Failure:</u> The Facet's energies rebound on the werewolf. He cannot attack anyone without a successful Resolve + Composure roll for the remainder of the scene.<br /> <br /> <u>Failure:</u> The Facet has no effect.<br /> <br /> <u>Success:</u> For the duration of the Facet, the victim is compelled to not attack the werewolf or any of his allies. He also suffers the Demoralized Condition. Attacking someone thus affected lifts their compulsion. This power doesn't works over those who are gripped by Death Rage.<br /> <br /> <u>Exceptional Success:</u> For the duration of the Facet, he also gains the Cowed Condition.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>The Height of Glory</u> [Glory]<br /> Cost:</b> 3 Essence<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> None<br /> <b>Action: </b>Reflexive<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Scene<br /> By invoking this Facet, the werewolf feels himself empowered to fight even with reckless abandon, trusting his heightened instincts to offer him some protection from harm. He adds his Glory Renown as a dice bonus when making all-out attacks, as well as a bonus to his Defense that persists even after he has performed an all-out attack. If the werewolf falls into Basu-Im, he can activate this Facet at no cost.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Relentless Focus</u> [Honor]<br /> Cost:</b> 3 Essence<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Resolve + Empathy + Honor<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> The Uratha using this Facet gains intense focus on whatever actions are most important to him, and only the greatest of temptations or distractions can gain his attention.<br /> <br /> <u>Dramatic Failure:</u> The Uratha not only fails to focus. He also throws his mind into a state of disorder. He gains the Distracted Condition for the scene.<br /> <br /> <u>Failure:</u> The Uratha cannot gain the desired level of focus.<br /> <br /> <u>Success:</u> For every success achieved on the roll, the werewolf can add his dots in Honor Renown whenever he spends a Willpower point to gain bonus dice in a single roll.<br /> <br /> <u>Exceptional Success:</u> In addition to the usual effects of a success, the werewolf gains the Inspired Condition.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Soul's Gaze</u> [Purity]</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>1 Essence<br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b>Intelligence + Investigation + Purity<br /> <b>Action: </b>Instant<br /> By gazing intently, the werewolf can judge another's soul.<br /> <br /> <u>Dramatic Failure:</u> The character receives a completely false idea on his target's mental state. He may mistake a high Harmony werewolf for the opposite, or incorrectly believes certain actions and situations may be possible breaking points.<br /> <br /> <u>Failure:</u> The Facet does not uncover any information.<br /> <br /> <u>Success:</u> The werewolf gets a sense of his target's mental state. For humans, this Facet reveals the strength of their psyche in terms of Integrity. For werewolves, it reveals how much they are (or are not) in tune with their dual nature according to their Harmony. Other supernaturals targeted by this Facet yield information according to their effective Integrity rating.<br /> <br /> <u>Exceptional Success:</u> In addition to the usual effects of the success, the werewolf gains several pieces of information equal to his Purity Renown. Such information pertains to his target's spiritual balance, and how it can be maintained or destroyed. This can be a given character's breaking points, or (when applicable) Touchstones.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Place of Serenity [Wisdom]</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>1 Essence<br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b>Composure + Empathy + Wisdom<br /> <b>Action: </b>Reflexive<br /> <b>Duration: </b>1 Day<br /> This Facet can be invoked after an Uratha has performed a successful meditation, strengthening his emotions with a bulwark of faith.<br /> <br /> <u>Dramatic Failure:</u> The Facet does the exact opposite, depriving the werewolf of any clarity of thought. He loses the benefits gained from meditating and suffers the Confused Condition.<br /> <br /> <u>Failure:</u> The werewolf gains the benefits of meditating, but nothing more than that.<br /> <br /> <u>Success:</u> In addition to the usual effects of meditation, the Werewolf gains a bonus to all Resolve + Composure rolls equal to his Wisdom Renown for the duration of the Facet's effects.<br /> <br /> <u>Exceptional Success</u>: The werewolf's mind is sharper, allowing him to think more clearly and better shake off distractions. He may ignore a number of circumstantial penalties equal to his Wisdom Renown for the duration of the Facet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 01-28-2016, 12:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T17:40:42-08:00","id":816535,"title":"","content":"Here's another Moon Gift, this time a partial conversion of the Dreaming Moon Gifts from 1st Edition. If anyone has critique - especially for the last Facet - I would deeply appreciate it. <hr /><br /> <u><b><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Gift of the Dreaming Moon</span></b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Waking Visions (o)</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> None (or 1 Essence)<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Permanent<br /> Those who first Changed under the Dreaming Moon are frequently struck with vivid dreams. By developing this Facet, the Cahalith becomes more attuned to her subconscious, receiving brief visions which warn her of impending danger. She may add his Glory Renown to all perception rolls, and to rolls made to detect ambushes and traps. If he chooses to spend Essence and roll the Facet's dice pool, the werewolf can extend her foresight, allowing her to divine impending events within a period of [Glory x4] hours.<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Wits + Occult + Glory<br /> <br /> <u>Dramatic Failure:</u> The player asks a question as though she had rolled a success; the Storyteller should either give false information, or present a warped version of the truth.<br /> <br /> <u>Failure:</u> The Cahalith's visions are too cryptic to decipher. She does not gain any information, though he may try again at a cumulative -1 penalty (to a maximum of -5).<br /> <br /> <u>Success:</u> The player can ask one question from the Storyteller. The Storyteller\u2019s answer should include the imagery conveyed by the visions.<br /> <br /> <u>Exceptional Success:</u> As a success, but the Cahalith automatically receives a vision relevant to the events he is experiencing. The Storyteller must reveal something relevant to the story, which the player can use to pose his question.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>One Voice</u> (oo)<br /> Cost:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Permanent<br /> With this Facet, a Cahalith can keep packmates in constant contact with one another. Pack members within a radius of 10 feet per dot of the Cahalith per dot of her Glory Renown are capable of instantaneous mental communication with one another. Any speaker can reach one particular packmate of his choice, or with all of them simultaneously. Connected characters also gain a bonus equal to the Cahalith's Glory on Initiative and on teamwork actions with one another, as they're better able to coordinate their efforts. The Facet cannot be used to communicate with packmates across the Gauntlet, or in a different plane of existence.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Farsighted Hunter</u> (ooo)<br /> Cost</b>: 1 Essence<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Duration:</b> The full duration of Siskur-Dah.<br /> To be a Cahalith is to be ridden by one's dreams, to sense things in sharp context, to have one's soul constantly churning with thoughts and impulses that demand expression. In the Hunt, her visions take a sharper focus, helping her to better guide her pack towards their prey. For the duration of the Facet, when invoking Waking Visions to peer into the future, the Cahalith may gain a number of insights on her prey equal to her Glory Renown. She may also spend a point of Essence once per night to receive a Prophetic Dream regarding the prey.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Aria of the Soul (oooo)<br /> Cost:</b> 2 Essence<br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b>Presence + Expression + Glory<br /> <b>Action:</b> Extended (25 successes; each roll represents one minute of singing)<br /> The Cahalith's art, the embodied howl, is capable of more than communication; the highest of the Gibbous Moons can not only communicate but commune. A soulsinger is able to draw on the power of the dreaming moon to soothe and heal, to wipe away a person's trauma and nightmares and replace them with gentle sleep.<br /> <br /> <u>Dramatic Failure:</u> The song goes horribly wrong, stirring up more terrible memories or visions and twisting them into sharp relief. The subject suffers the Soul Shocked Condition.<br /> <br /> <u>Failure:</u> The Uratha gains no successes, and gains the Stumbled Condition.<br /> <br /> <u>Success:</u> Successes are gained; if the total reaches 25 successes or more, the song insinuates fully into the mind and memory of the subject. What the subject experiences is left to the Storyteller's discretion, but usually the song either assuages the pain of a terrible memory or reminds the subject of a sweeter memory that has been recently repressed by more terrible experiences. The song cannot permanently heal mental scars, but it can soothe them for a time. The subject does not suffer from the effects of any negative emotion- or mind-based Conditions he has until the next moon phase, unless they are resolved before the Facet ends.<br /> <br /> Performing the Facet once in a given lunar phase is a breaking point for the werewolf at a -3 penalty. The power helps to center his dual nature even as it soothes the soul of his target. If he's cleaving to the World of Flesh, the breaking point is one towards Spirit. The same is true vice versa. Other werewolves who hear the song also experience the breaking point if they are hearing it for the first time in a given phase.<br /> <br /> <u>Exceptional Success:</u> Successes are gained; if the total reaches 30 successes or more, the song is particularly potent. The werewolf and all witnesses to his performance regain a point of Willpower for every success above 30.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Hunter's Dream (ooooo)</b><br /> No matter the distance that separates them, the whole pack always meet in their dreams, securing a territory deep in the Astral Realms. A Cahalith with this Facet develops an Astral Den, which functions similarly to a Beast's Lair with regards to its environment. Here, packmates can convene secretly without too much suspicion, though the Cahalith has the right to bar entry to any member of the pack.<br /> <br /> ===============<br /> <b>Sidebar: Astral Den</b><br /> Mechanically similar to a Beast's Lair, the Astral Den uses half the Cahalith's Primal Urge (rounded up) as its effective Lair rating. It also possesses Chambers and Lair Traits, though the Cahalith is restricted only to Minor Traits for the latter.<br /> <br /> Members of the pack may access the Den whenever they are either sleeping or in a trance-like state. They manifest in a Dream Form, with the Cahalith using the highest among her Attributes to determine her Power, Finesse, and Resistance. If a member of the pack is prevented from entering for any reason by the Gibbous Moon, he may trigger a Clash of Wills, rolling his Primal Urge and the higher of his Auspice or Tribal Renown as a dice pool. Mortal and Wolf-Blooded members cannot contest the ban, and may only be granted entry by the Cahalith's consent.<br /> <br /> A Cahalith can also physically enter her Lair by opening a portal similar to a Beast's Primordial Pathways. Doing so, however, must be done in a location resonant to the Den. And the act itself is an Extended Action, with a target number of 30 successes (each roll representing 10 minutes). The Cahalith also spends Essence equal to [6 - her Honorary Rank] in <i>addition to</i> a Willpower point.<br /> ===============","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":".  Slight updates to Hunter's Dream 03-11-2017, 06:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T04:44:55-08:00","id":816774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=816535#post816535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Aria of the Soul (oooo)</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I would add that, once a month, hearing this song is a breaking point towards the center of Uratha's Harmony. If she is too much flesh, she becomes more spirit, and vice-versa.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T05:01:16-08:00","id":816785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BinAly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=816774#post816774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would add that, once a month, hearing this song is a breaking point towards the center of Uratha's Harmony. If she is too much flesh, she becomes more spirit, and vice-versa.</div> </div> </div> </div>How about hearing <i>or</i> performing the song? So, it'd be written that...<br /> <br /> &quot;Performing the Facet once in a lunar month is a breaking point for the werewolf at a -3 penalty. The power helps to center his dual nature even as it soothes the soul of his target. If he's cleaving to the World of Flesh, the breaking point is one towards Spirit. The same is true vice versa. Other werewolves who hear the song also experience the breaking point if they are hearing it for the first time in a month.&quot;.<br /> <br /> That said, you got any suggestions for the fifth Facet? Or any critique for the others? I was considering a power in the form of a howl which forces all those who hear it to be rendered unconscious, or at least stunned/insensate. And at the same time, I'm trying to decide on an Essence cost for Hunter's Dream.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 01-26-2016, 08:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T05:45:10-08:00","id":816807,"title":"","content":"Finally added the fifth Facet, a reskinned Howl of Nightmares that's been renamed &quot;Lunatic Pandora&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T06:16:20-08:00","id":816823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=816785#post816785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How about hearing <i>or</i> performing the song? So, it'd be written that...<br /> <br /> &quot;Performing the Facet once in a lunar month is a breaking point for the werewolf at a -3 penalty. The power helps to center his dual nature even as it soothes the soul of his target. If he's cleaving to the World of Flesh, the breaking point is one towards Spirit. The same is true vice versa. Other werewolves who hear the song also experience the breaking point if they are hearing it for the first time in a month.&quot;.<br /> <br /> That said, you got any suggestions for the fifth Facet? Or any critique for the others? I was considering a power in the form of a howl which forces all those who hear it to be rendered unconscious, or at least stunned/insensate. And at the same time, I'm trying to decide on an Essence cost for Hunter's Dream.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have nothing against letting the performer benefit from the power.<br /> <br /> As soon as my work allows me, I'm going to deliver feedback on all Facets. As for your initial thinking on the fifth, wouldn't that be too similar to the new gift described in the Blog? The one that removes the soul of the targets and gives it to the Cahalith. Removing a soul makes the target mad at long term.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Soul Shriek (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">The Cahalith unleashes a banshee scream of raw, primal madness.</span></span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><b>Cost:</b> 3 Essence</span></span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><b>Dice Pool:</b> Presence + Intimidate + Glory vs. Composure + Primal Urge</span></span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><b>Action:</b> Instant</span></span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><b>Roll Results</b></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The Cahalith gains the Stunned Tilt.</span></span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><b>Failure:</b> The Facet fails.</span></span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><b>Success: </b>Any werewolf or spirit prey who hears the howl and fails to roll as many successes as the Cahalith is struck with the Essence Overload Condition. Other prey who fails to roll as many successes as the Cahalith suffers the Soulless Condition as his soul tears free from his body. Souls taken in this way are in the werewolf\u2019s possession, appearing about her person as floating spirit-lanterns or shards of light that are visible when she flares her Renown or is in the Shadow. The Cahalith\u2019s death or her willing agreement will restore the lost soul.</span></span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><b>Exceptional Success:</b> Prey suffers the Enervated Condition rather than the Soulless Condition.</span></span></span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> What about playing with Oneiros and Astral Plane? Since this is a very dream focused Gift, it seems that it could work. Maybe sucking everyone into a nightmare controlled by the user? Maybe entering the dream of a target and affecting it somewhat? Or something like a Dream Eater, which infects targets and recovers Willpower in their place.<br /> <br /> What about transforming the target into a Sleep-Walker packmember? Controlling sleep-walkers and using them as you please.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T06:25:54-08:00","id":816826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BinAly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=816823#post816823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have nothing against letting the performer benefit from the power.<br /> <br /> As soon as my work allows me, I'm going to deliver feedback on all Facets. As for your initial thinking on the fifth, wouldn't that be too similar to the new gift described in the Blog? The one that removes the soul of the targets and gives it to the Cahalith. Removing a soul makes the target mad at long term.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. You may have a point there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BinAly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=816823#post816823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about playing with Oneiros and Astral Plane? Since this is a very dream focused Gift, it seems that it could work. Maybe sucking everyone into a nightmare controlled by the user? Maybe entering the dream of a target and affecting it somewhat? Or something like a Dream Eater, which infects targets and recovers Willpower in their place.<br /> <br /> What about transforming the target into a Sleep-Walker packmember? Controlling sleep-walkers and using them as you please.</div> </div> </div> </div>The ability to enter and affect another's dreams (a la Oneiromancy and/or Oneiromachy) was something I was contemplating as an alternative to Lover's Voice. But then again, it probably has a high utility that would make it better suited as a five-dot Facet.<br /> <br /> As for the bit on Dream Eaters, could you elaborate on that, when you can?<br /> <br /> The ability to transform a target into a sleepwalking packmember is also another interesting concept. But perhaps an alternative could be that it's a Facet for a Shadow Gift of Dreams/Sleep?<br /> <br /> Regarding the other Facets, I was thinking of amping up the rolled aspect of Waking Visions to be less like Auspex and more like the kith blessing of the Oracle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 01-26-2016, 09:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T07:26:11-08:00","id":816857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=816826#post816826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the bit on Dream Eaters, could you elaborate on that, when you can?</div> </div> </div> </div>Roughly, I imagine a power that allows the user to mark a target, and while marked, everytime the target should recover Willpower through sleep, it instead goes to the user in the form of Essence. The target is afflicted by powerful nightmares where she sees the user devouring her repeatedly, and can't rest properly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=816826#post816826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The ability to transform a target into a sleepwalking packmember is also another interesting concept. But perhaps an alternative could be that it's a Facet for a Shadow Gift of Dreams/Sleep?</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough, I will probably design something like that myself because the idea is very interesting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=816826#post816826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding the other Facets, I was thinking of amping up the rolled aspect of Waking Visions to be less like Auspex and more like the kith blessing of the Oracle.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not familiar with the blessing of the Oracle, what are the main differences you want to achieve?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T07:45:40-08:00","id":816869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BinAly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=816857#post816857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Roughly, I imagine a power that allows the user to mark a target, and while marked, every time the target should recover Willpower through sleep, it instead goes to the user in the form of Essence. The target is afflicted by powerful nightmares where she sees the user devouring her repeatedly, and can't rest properly.</div> </div> </div> </div>It likely could fit as the Cunning Facet of a possible Gift of Dreams/Sleep, while the one with sleepwalking pack members could fit as a Wisdom Facet.<br /> <br /> That said, I think I'll go with the five-dot Facet of Dreaming Moon allowing the Cahalith to perform oneiromancy/oneiromachy on a target. What do you think?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BinAly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=816857#post816857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not familiar with the blessing of the Oracle, what are the main differences you want to achieve?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the kith blessing, from the development draft. What I was thinking of emulating has been highlighted in italics.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Blessing:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The character regularly catches glimpses of the next second or two. He gains +5 to Initiative, +1 to Defense, and gains one free success on any rolls to detect ambushes (see p. XX).<i> If he spends a point of Glamour, he can look further into the future and can ask yes or no questions about the most likely future of a single person, place, or object, such as whether a murder will occur in a location in the day. In secret, the Storyteller rolls the character\u2019s Wits + Occult. For each success, she must answer a question correctly. She does not tell the player when her successes have \u201crun out\u201d. The player can only ask about the future of a single target once per day.</i></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T13:04:43-08:00","id":817084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=816869#post816869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It likely could fit as the Cunning Facet of a possible Gift of Dreams/Sleep, while the one with sleepwalking pack members could fit as a Wisdom Facet.<br /> <br /> That said, I think I'll go with the five-dot Facet of Dreaming Moon allowing the Cahalith to perform oneiromancy/oneiromachy on a target. What do you think?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing against it, but it needs to feel powerful and have a very profound effect. Maybe you could add or remove &quot;Glory&quot; from a Destiny Merit? The Player would chose something to be the end of the prophecy. You could limit it's power by saying that this prophecy only lasts until the next moon-phase currently in the sky.<br /> <br /> By Destiny I mean giving bonuses to actions that go directly in favor of the prophecy and penalties to actions against it. A condition that gives a new aspiration and new beat opportunities if following the destiny would be awesome too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=816869#post816869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If he spends a point of Glamour, he can look further into the future and can ask yes or no questions about the most likely future of a single person, place, or object, such as whether a murder will occur in a location in the day. In secret, the Storyteller rolls the character\u2019s Wits + Occult. For each success, she must answer a question correctly. She does not tell the player when her successes have \u201crun out\u201d. The player can only ask about the future of a single target once per day.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds good. Maybe to make it a little different from the original, you can limit the maximum prediction to &quot;within the scene&quot;, not the whole day, or &quot;Glory&quot;*&quot;X&quot;hours, making it predict a full day only at the peak of Glory. Also, it could be just one question, no matter how many successes you achieved. Exceptional success could grant an automatic relevant vision, with the storyteller informing something relevant to the story even if the character did not made the right question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T14:40:34-08:00","id":817184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=816535#post816535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If anyone has critique - especially for the last Facet - I would deeply appreciate it.</div> </div> </div> </div> My initial impression is that the Gift name doesn't really match the content. It doesn't feel very... dream-related, symbolically or practically.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Waking Visions (o)</b> </div> </div> </div> Excessively vague. The dice bonus is nice, albeit limited, but gaining 'insights' could either be incredibly powerful or utterly useless depending on what insights *are*.\u200b Needs more definition as to what info etc it can convey on threats and weaknesses, and ideally needs to avoid crossover with existing Facets on that front. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <u><b>Lover's Voice (oo)</b></u> </div> </div> </div> Mimicking a voice seems a pretty minor power, doesn't feel like something for a 'Dreaming Moon' list and doesn't do a *lot* towards making the Cahalith a better hunter; I mean, it does a bit, but it's very underwhelming.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> [B]Hunter's Dream (ooo) </div> </div> </div> Again, doesn't feel like it matches 'Dreaming Moon'. Otherwise not too bad power-wise but I'd need to double-check Steadfast and Inspired. Also sometimes you *want* to suffer breaking points on the hunt since they're bringing you closer to balance rather than further away.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Aria of the Soul (oooo)</b> </div> </div> </div> I am really really wary of any power that is basically 'full Willpower refill', which is what this is. It takes time and requires the target to pass some trivial rolls to stay conscious (unless the werewolf is an utter weakling and even then doesn't want to shift to, say, Urshul for the extra Stamina), but that's not enough of a drawback for the capability to directly shunt Essence into Willpower as needed. It suspends Conditions but not all Conditions are necessarily internal and mental and, more importantly, some Conditions are flat-out beneficial and you don't *want* them relieved for a month.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Lunatic Pandora (ooooo)</b> </div> </div> </div> Thematically this might work if the other powers really gave the Dreaming feel to the Dreaming Moon list, but they don't so this doesn't really convey the nightmares side of things as it has no foundation to rest on. Why can the Facet only be used once per scene? Doesn't it overlap too much with Soul Shriek and Thousand Throat Howl?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T16:30:24-08:00","id":817236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=817184#post817184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My initial impression is that the Gift name doesn't really match the content. It doesn't feel very... dream-related, symbolically or practically.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the main issue might be the focus on prophecy and illusion instead of sleep, dreams and nightmares. Also, since the standard moon gift already has a &quot;Dream Hunter&quot; facet, it is difficult to not overlap, quite a challenge.<br /> <br /> Here is a brief summary of what the Gibbous Gifts already cover:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Rank 1:</b> Inspire to Violence, Freeze from Fear <span style=\"color:#A9A9A9\">(Increased Violence for Allies <i>and</i> Initiative Penalties for Enemies)</span><br /> <br /> <b>Rank 2:</b> Superb Warleader, Superb Intimidation <span style=\"color:#A9A9A9\">(Increased Capacity to Incite Violence <i>and</i> Increased Capacity to Incite Fear)</span><br /> <br /> <b>Rank 3:</b> Dream Hunter, Maddening Visage <span style=\"color:#A9A9A9\">(Weakening Willpower from Sleeping Prey <i>and</i> Weakening Prey's Ability to Maintain Sanity (all during the Siskur-Dah))</span><br /> <br /> <b>Rank 4:</b> Monstrous Opponent, Lingering Madness <span style=\"color:#A9A9A9\">(Initiative and Emotional Penalties to Prey and Powerful Mental Conditions, Fugue and Amnesia)</span><br /> <br /> <b>Rank 5</b>: Ultimate Trapper, Soul Eater <span style=\"color:#A9A9A9\">(Diminishes Prey's Capacity to Escape and Removes the Soul, damning the prey to certain madness)</span></span> </div> </div> </div>This might help measuring which powers overlap. Also, I believe we should mostly depart from violence oriented powers, since there are many. To be unique, the Dream Gift seems to need more subtle facets.<br /> <br /> (edited for readability)<br /> <br /> (edited again to add: I believe we already have sufficient feedback to work. I will refrain from criticizing until we fix the issues pointed by Acrozatarim)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5446,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","user":"BinAly","date":". 01-26-2016, 07:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T20:11:04-08:00","id":817358,"title":"","content":"<b>Waking Visions (o)</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=817184#post817184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Excessively vague. The dice bonus is nice, albeit limited, but gaining 'insights' could either be incredibly powerful or utterly useless depending on what insights *are*.\u200b Needs more definition as to what info etc it can convey on threats and weaknesses, and ideally needs to avoid crossover with existing Facets on that front.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BinAly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=817084#post817084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe to make it a little different from the original, you can limit the maximum prediction to &quot;within the scene&quot;, not the whole day, or &quot;Glory&quot;*&quot;X&quot;hours, making it predict a full day only at the peak of Glory. Also, it could be just one question, no matter how many successes you achieved. Exceptional success could grant an automatic relevant vision, with the storyteller informing something relevant to the story even if the character did not made the right question.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps I could expand the dice bonus to all perception rolls in addition to rolls to detecting ambushes and traps?<br /> <br /> I'm probably going to go with BinAly's suggestion that the prediction be limited to within a period of several hours equal to the Cahalith's Glory Renown. As well as maybe even one question on a success (with the exceptional success granting a relevant vision on which to word your question for extra information). What I was thinking of going for this aspect of the Facet was something that mimicked the 2E Oracle's Blessing and/or the Auspex Discipline's first two dots.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b>Lover's Voice (oo)</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=817184#post817184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mimicking a voice seems a pretty minor power, doesn't feel like something for a 'Dreaming Moon' list and doesn't do a *lot* towards making the Cahalith a better hunter; I mean, it does a bit, but it's very underwhelming.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then, how about giving the Cahalith the ability to perform oneiromancy and oneiromachy? Of course, that Facet would probably need an update once Changeling 2E is out.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b>Hunter's Dream (ooo)</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=817184#post817184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, doesn't feel like it matches 'Dreaming Moon'. Otherwise not too bad power-wise but I'd need to double-check Steadfast and Inspired. Also sometimes you *want* to suffer breaking points on the hunt since they're bringing you closer to balance rather than further away.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe remove that bonus on breaking points, then? The reason I worded it like this was that the Gift of the Dreaming Moon's themes are prophect, illusions, <i>and</i> inspiration. The last refers specifically to how the Cahalith is supposed to inspire the pack to greater heights of glory, heights that are the stuff of dreams and legends.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b>Aria of the Soul (oooo)</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=817184#post817184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am really really wary of any power that is basically 'full Willpower refill', which is what this is. It takes time and requires the target to pass some trivial rolls to stay conscious (unless the werewolf is an utter weakling and even then doesn't want to shift to, say, Urshul for the extra Stamina), but that's not enough of a drawback for the capability to directly shunt Essence into Willpower as needed. It suspends Conditions but not all Conditions are necessarily internal and mental and, more importantly, some Conditions are flat-out beneficial and you don't *want* them relieved for a month.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe I have to specify that the Conditions this Facet relieves are emotional/mental <i>and</i> negative in nature. Plus, I could remove that roll to stay conscious since it might seem forced. Otherwise, perhaps restrictions to how many times the Facet is used can be considered. Maybe even a raised Essence cost.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b>Lunatic Pandora (ooooo)</b><br /> <br /> Scrapping this one to imagine a new fifth Facet for the Gift. You aren't wrong in saying that it overlaps with Soul Shriek and Thousand Throat Howl in some ways.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BinAly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=817084#post817084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe you could add or remove &quot;Glory&quot; from a Destiny Merit? The Player would chose something to be the end of the prophecy. You could limit it's power by saying that this prophecy only lasts until the next moon-phase currently in the sky.<br /> <br /> By Destiny I mean giving bonuses to actions that go directly in favor of the prophecy and penalties to actions against it. A condition that gives a new aspiration and new beat opportunities if following the destiny would be awesome too.</div> </div> </div> </div>This could inspire a replacement for Lover's Voice. And that should free up the oneiromancy/oneiromachy Facet to be the five-dot one for the Gift. Would that work?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T23:35:57-08:00","id":817433,"title":"","content":"Well everyone has already said the things, but that one Fervor Gift you made where you add Glory to all out attacks for 3 essence and a roll and in an instant action seems flat out inferior to Primal Strength. Might be a bit steep. I guess the potential exceptional success is an advantage, but still. Seems odd to have to roll, then pay so much more for a more limited version of a gift that already exists, and not even as a reflexive action. I think it's called Height of Glory.<br /> <br /> I would suggest also that the Fervor facets actually be not restricted to the gift user, but able to used on other targets. That might justify using the Glory Facet over Primal Strength - though that's what Reflected Facets is for (if that was already the intent, I don't think it's completely clear).<br /> <br /> Otherwise I really like them. Maybe allow the Purity one to force a breaking point? (toward harmony) Since it might need a bit more functionality to feel effective. I really like the Cunning one. Not sure about the renown fit itself, but i can already think of a bunch of fun uses of it.<br /> <br /> That's all. Fervor (and Disease) was one of my favourite gifts, though I couldn't tell you why. Glad you chose it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T00:06:13-08:00","id":817442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=817433#post817433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well everyone has already said the things, but that one Fervor Gift you made where you add Glory to all out attacks for 3 essence and a roll and in an instant action seems flat out inferior to Primal Strength. Might be a bit steep. I guess the potential exceptional success is an advantage, but still. Seems odd to have to roll, then pay so much more for a more limited version of a gift that already exists, and not even as a reflexive action. I think it's called Height of Glory.<br /> <br /> I would suggest also that the Fervor facets actually be not restricted to the gift user, but able to used on other targets. That might justify using the Glory Facet over Primal Strength - though that's what Reflected Facets is for (if that was already the intent, I don't think it's completely clear).<br /> <br /> Otherwise I really like them. Maybe allow the Purity one to force a breaking point? (toward harmony) Since it might need a bit more functionality to feel effective. I really like the Cunning one. Not sure about the renown fit itself, but i can already think of a bunch of fun uses of it.<br /> <br /> That's all. Fervor (and Disease) was one of my favourite gifts, though I couldn't tell you why. Glad you chose it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good idea. I'll see if I can revise the Facets, as needed. As for Height of Glory, how about something like this?<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b><u>The Height of Glory</u> [Glory]<br /> Cost:</b> 3 Essence<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> None<br /> <b>Action: </b>Reflexive<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Scene<br /> By invoking this Facet, the werewolf feels himself empowered to fight even with reckless abandon, trusting his heightened instincts to offer him some protection from harm. He adds his Glory Renown as a dice bonus when making all-out attacks, as well as a bonus to his Defense that persists even after he has performed an all-out attack. If the werewolf falls into Basu-Im, he can activate this Facet at no cost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 01-27-2016, 05:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T22:37:45-08:00","id":818218,"title":"","content":"Here's my revision of the first Dreaming Moon Facet.<br /> <br /> <b>-=-<br /> <br /> Waking Visions (o)</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> None (or 1 Essence)<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Permanent<br /> Those who first Changed under the Dreaming Moon are frequently struck with vivid dreams. By developing this Facet, the Cahalith becomes more attuned to her subconscious, receiving brief visions which warn her of impending danger. She may add his Glory Renown to all perception rolls, and to rolls made to detect ambushes and traps. If he chooses to spend Essence and roll the Facet's dice pool, the werewolf can extend her foresight, allowing her to divine impending events within a period of [Glory x4] hours.<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Wits + Empathy + Glory<br /> <br /> <u>Dramatic Failure:</u> The player asks a question as though she had rolled a success; the Storyteller should either give false information, or present a warped version of the truth.<br /> <br /> <u>Failure:</u> The Cahalith's visions are too cryptic to decipher. She does not gain any information, though he may try again at a cumulative -1 penalty (to a maximum of -5).<br /> <br /> <u>Success:</u> The player can ask one question from the Storyteller. The Storyteller\u2019s answer should include the imagery conveyed by the visions.<br /> <br /> <u>Exceptional Success:</u> As a success, but the Cahalith automatically receives a vision relevant to the events he is experiencing. The Storyteller must reveal something relevant to the story, which the player can use to pose his question.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> Alternatively, I was thinking of making the Facet allow for the player to ask a number of questions equal to her Glory Renown. And maybe extend the temporal range of the power to within a day, or even a week or (lunar) month? Thoughts?<br /> <br /> Below is the old version.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Waking Visions (o)<br /> Cost:</b> 1 Essence<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Scene<br /> Those who first Changed under the Dreaming Moon are frequently struck with vivid dreams. By developing this Facet, the Cahalith becomes more attuned to her subconscious, receiving brief visions which warn her of impending danger. She may add his Glory Renown to all perception rolls made to detect ambushes and traps. If he chooses to roll the Facet's dice pool, the werewolf can glean insights on her immediate surroundings.<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Wits + Empathy + Glory<br /> <br /> <u>Dramatic Failure:</u> The player asks a question as though she had rolled a success; the Storyteller should either give false information, or present a warped version of the truth.<br /> <br /> <u>Failure:</u> The Cahalith's visions are too cryptic to decipher. She does not gain any information, though he may try again at a cumulative -1 penalty (to a maximum of -5).<br /> <br /> <u>Success:</u> The player can ask one question per success from the Storyteller. The Storyteller\u2019s answer should include the imagery conveyed by the visions. The Facet can only answer immediate questions pertaining to threats and weaknesses.<br /> <br /> <u>Exceptional Success:</u> No additional effects.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Alternatively, if we go for the [Glory] Hours bit, I have another way to determine its temporal range.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 500px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Glory Renown</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Temporal Range</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">1</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Hour/Scene</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">3 Hours</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">3</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">6 Hours</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">4</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">12 Hours</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">1 Day</td> </tr> </table></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 01-28-2016, 01:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T22:48:53-08:00","id":818222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=817433#post817433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well everyone has already said the things, but that one Fervor Gift you made where you add Glory to all out attacks for 3 essence and a roll and in an instant action seems flat out inferior to Primal Strength. Might be a bit steep. I guess the potential exceptional success is an advantage, but still. Seems odd to have to roll, then pay so much more for a more limited version of a gift that already exists, and not even as a reflexive action. I think it's called Height of Glory.<br /> <br /> I would suggest also that the Fervor facets actually be not restricted to the gift user, but able to used on other targets. That might justify using the Glory Facet over Primal Strength - though that's what Reflected Facets is for (if that was already the intent, I don't think it's completely clear).<br /> <br /> Otherwise I really like them. Maybe allow the Purity one to force a breaking point? (toward harmony) Since it might need a bit more functionality to feel effective. I really like the Cunning one. Not sure about the renown fit itself, but i can already think of a bunch of fun uses of it.<br /> <br /> That's all. Fervor (and Disease) was one of my favourite gifts, though I couldn't tell you why. Glad you chose it.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=806016#post806016\">Added the revision to the Gift of Fervor.</a> But I'm still trying to figure out how to amp up Soul's Gaze. Maybe make the ability to read one's (effective) Integrity be a passive like Barghest, the Death Gift's Glory Facet? And the dice pool could be something that inflicts, perhaps, the Soul Shocked Condition from Beast: The Primordial? Or perhaps the Abruption Condition?<br /> <br /> Any more suggestions? Oh, and the old version of Height of Glory is below this post for reference purposes.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b><u>The Height of Glory</u> [Glory]<br /> Cost:</b> 3 Essence<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Strength + Expression + Glory<br /> <b>Action: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Scene<br /> By invoking the power of this Facet, the werewolf is buoyed with a surge of faith that lend power to his strikes whenever he chooses not to hold back.<br /> <br /> <u>Dramatic Failure:</u> The werewolf is struck by doubt and despair, fearing for his life. For the duration of the scene, he gains the Frightened Condition related to fighting. He cannot take no action in battle except to dodge.<br /> <br /> <u>Failure:</u> The Facet confers no effects.<br /> <br /> <u>Success:</u> The werewolf feels himself be empowered whenever he fights with reckless abandon. For the duration of the Facet, the Werewolf adds his Glory Renown as a dice bonus when making all-out attacks. They still lose their Defense, as usual.<br /> <br /> <u>Exceptional Success:</u> In addition to its usual effects, the Facet enables the werewolf to avoid the worst of any attacks made against him as he rampages. He adds his Glory Renown to his Defense, and continues to apply it even while making all-out attacks.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 01-28-2016, 01:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T02:26:35-08:00","id":818302,"title":"","content":"<b>Lapse of Faith</b> making you potentially betray your pack without so much as providing a beat? No. Normal success should apply the <i>Demoralized</i> condition, without a need for physical assault, make the roll use expression so the character is shaken socially.<br /> <br /> An exceptional success could also apply the<i> Cowed</i> condition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T05:07:34-08:00","id":818342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=818302#post818302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Lapse of Faith</b> making you potentially betray your pack without so much as providing a beat? No. Normal success should apply the <i>Demoralized</i> condition, without a need for physical assault, make the roll use expression so the character is shaken socially.<br /> <br /> An exceptional success could also apply the <i>Cowed</i> condition.</div> </div> </div> </div>How about this?<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Lapse of Faith</u> [Cunning]<br /> Cost:</b> 1 Essence<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Presence + Expression + Cunning vs. Resolve + Primal Urge<br /> <b>Action:</b> Reflexive and Contested<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Scene<br /> The werewolf can force a spiritual compulsion that hinders her prey's attempts at fighting back against him. It can potentially even force him to turn on those he's fighting alongside.<br /> <br /> <u>Dramatic Failure:</u> The Facet's energies rebound on the werewolf. He cannot attack anyone without a successful Resolve + Composure roll for the remainder of the scene.<br /> <br /> <u>Failure:</u> The Facet has no effect.<br /> <br /> <u>Success:</u> For the duration of the Facet, the victim is compelled to not attack the werewolf or any of his allies. He suffers the Demoralized Condition.<br /> <br /> <u>Exceptional Success:</u> The victim now feels compelled to aid the werewolf, even to the point of attacking his family, friends or pack. For the duration of the Facet, he now gains the Cowed Condition, as well as the Obsession Condition towards her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T08:49:58-08:00","id":818469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=818218#post818218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alternatively, I was thinking of making the Facet allow for the player to ask a number of questions equal to her Glory Renown. And maybe extend the temporal range of the power to within a day, or even a week or (lunar) month? Thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Changing this Facet to be a &quot;month&quot; prediction seems to simply make it another use of the Auspice default ability, doesn't it?<br /> <br /> If we are going to keep the theme of prophecy, we should consider changing the name of the Gift to a better match. Something along the lines of Gift of the Pregnant Moon or Gift of Moon Gazer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T09:02:11-08:00","id":818475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BinAly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=818469#post818469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changing this Facet to be a &quot;month&quot; prediction seems to simply make it another use of the Auspice default ability, doesn't it?<br /> <br /> If we are going to keep the theme of prophecy, we should consider changing the name of the Gift to a better match. Something along the lines of Gift of the Pregnant Moon or Gift of Moon Gazer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, we could go for this scaling according to Renown, as you suggested?<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table_text_table\" style=\"width: 500px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_text_table_td\">Glory Renown</td> <td class=\"text_table_text_table_td\">Temporal Range</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_text_table_td\">1</td> <td class=\"text_table_text_table_td\">Hour/Scene</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_text_table_td\">2</td> <td class=\"text_table_text_table_td\">3 Hours</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_text_table_td\">3</td> <td class=\"text_table_text_table_td\">6 Hours</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_text_table_td\">4</td> <td class=\"text_table_text_table_td\">12 Hours</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_text_table_td\">5</td> <td class=\"text_table_text_table_td\">1 Day</td> </tr> </table></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T09:38:26-08:00","id":818508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=818342#post818342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How about this?<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Lapse of Faith</u> [Cunning]<br /> Cost:</b> 1 Essence<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Presence + Expression + Cunning vs. Resolve + Primal Urge<br /> <b>Action:</b> Reflexive and Contested<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Scene<br /> The werewolf can force a spiritual compulsion that hinders her prey's attempts at fighting back against him. It can potentially even force him to turn on those he's fighting alongside.<br /> <br /> <u>Dramatic Failure:</u> The Facet's energies rebound on the werewolf. He cannot attack anyone without a successful Resolve + Composure roll for the remainder of the scene.<br /> <br /> <u>Failure:</u> The Facet has no effect.<br /> <br /> <u>Success:</u> For the duration of the Facet, the victim is compelled to not attack the werewolf or any of his allies. He also suffers the Demoralized Condition. Attacking someone thus affected lifts their compulsion. This power doesn't works over those who are gripped by Death Rage.<br /> <br /> <u>Exceptional Success:</u> For the duration of the Facet, he also gains the Cowed Condition.</div> </div> </div> </div>This would be my take. Not even Kuruth can force you to attack your packmates if they fall on it as well. Lapse of Faith's exceptional effect would be more potent than several dominate effects otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T09:47:11-08:00","id":818518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=818508#post818508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This would be my take. Not even Kuruth can force you to attack your packmates if they fall on it as well. Lapse of Faith's exceptional effect would be more potent than several dominate effects otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Revising it, then <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Thanks for the critique on this Facet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T09:51:03-08:00","id":818525,"title":"","content":"Made the revision to the Cunning Facet of the Fervor Gift.<br /> <br /> Here's the previous version for those who are curious...<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b><u>Lapse of Faith</u> [Cunning]<br /> Cost:</b> 1 Essence<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Presence + Persuasion + Cunning vs. Resolve + Primal Urge<br /> <b>Action:</b> Reflexive and Contested<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Scene<br /> With a single bite, the werewolf can force a spiritual compulsion that hinders her prey's attempts at fighting back against him. It can potentially even force him to turn on those he's fighting alongside.<br /> <br /> <u>Dramatic Failure:</u> The Facet's energies rebound on the werewolf. He cannot attack anyone without a successful Resolve + Composure roll for the remainder of the scene.<br /> <br /> <u>Failure:</u> The Facet has no effect.<br /> <br /> <u>Success:</u> For the duration of the Facet, the victum is compelled to not attack the werewolf or any of his allies. Any attempt to do so requires a Resolve + Composure roll penalized by the werewolf's Cunning Renown.<br /> <br /> <u>Exceptional Success:</u> The victim now feels compelled to aid the Fire-Touched, even to the point of attacking her family, friends or pack. He now gains the Obsession Condition related to this for the duration of the Facet.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T11:04:37-08:00","id":818582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=818475#post818475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, we could go for this scaling according to Renown, as you suggested?<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table_text_table\" style=\"width: 500px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_text_table_td\">Glory Renown</td> <td class=\"text_table_text_table_td\">Temporal Range</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_text_table_td\">1</td> <td class=\"text_table_text_table_td\">Hour/Scene</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_text_table_td\">2</td> <td class=\"text_table_text_table_td\">3 Hours</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_text_table_td\">3</td> <td class=\"text_table_text_table_td\">6 Hours</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_text_table_td\">4</td> <td class=\"text_table_text_table_td\">12 Hours</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_text_table_td\">5</td> <td class=\"text_table_text_table_td\">1 Day</td> </tr> </table></div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have no problem with your first approach of 4 hours*Glory, simpler math is always good. I was just pointing out at your wish to extend the time-scale of the prediction even more, which for me, clashes a bit with the standard Cahalith ability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T17:29:40-08:00","id":818865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BinAly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=818582#post818582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have no problem with your first approach of 4 hours*Glory, simpler math is always good. I was just pointing out at your wish to extend the time-scale of the prediction even more, which for me, clashes a bit with the standard Cahalith ability.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright, then. I'll go with that.<br /> Do you think I should limit use of that aspect of the Facet to once per scene?<br /> <br /> And what do you think of me making the two-dot Facet allowing for the Cahalith to perform Oneiromancy and Oneiromachy?<br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b> Actually, I went for a different concept. What do you think?<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b><u>One Voice</u> (oo)<br /> Cost:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Permanent<br /> With this Facet, a Cahalith can keep packmates in constant contact with one another. Pack members within a radius of 10 feet per dot of the Cahalith per dot of her Glory Renown are capable of instantaneous mental communication with one another. Any speaker can reach one particular packmate of his choice, or with all of them simultaneously. Connected characters also gain a bonus equal to the Cahalith's Glory on Initiative and on teamwork actions with one another, as they're better able to coordinate their efforts. The Facet cannot be used to communicate with packmates across the Gauntlet, or in a different plane of existence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 01-28-2016, 11:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T20:28:04-08:00","id":818960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=817184#post817184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am really really wary of any power that is basically 'full Willpower refill', which is what this is. It takes time and requires the target to pass some trivial rolls to stay conscious (unless the werewolf is an utter weakling and even then doesn't want to shift to, say, Urshul for the extra Stamina), but that's not enough of a drawback for the capability to directly shunt Essence into Willpower as needed. It suspends Conditions but not all Conditions are necessarily internal and mental and, more importantly, some Conditions are flat-out beneficial and you don't *want* them relieved for a month.</div> </div> </div> </div>How about this? Is this better? Or perhaps I should limit the Willpower point gained by the exceptional success to just one point?<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b>Aria of the Soul (oooo)<br /> Cost:</b> 2 Essence<br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b>Presence + Expression + Glory<br /> <b>Action:</b> Extended (25 successes; each roll represents one minute of singing)<br /> The Cahalith's art, the embodied howl, is capable of more than communication; the highest of the Gibbous Moons can not only communicate but commune. A soulsinger is able to draw on the power of the dreaming moon to soothe and heal, to wipe away a person's trauma and nightmares and replace them with gentle sleep.<br /> <br /> <u>Dramatic Failure:</u> The song goes horribly wrong, stirring up more terrible memories or visions and twisting them into sharp relief. The subject suffers the Soul Shocked Condition.<br /> <br /> <u>Failure:</u> The Uratha gains no successes, and gains the Stumbled Condition.<br /> <br /> <u>Success:</u> Successes are gained; if the total reaches 25 successes or more, the song insinuates fully into the mind and memory of the subject. What the subject experiences is left to the Storyteller's discretion, but usually the song either assuages the pain of a terrible memory or reminds the subject of a sweeter memory that has been recently repressed by more terrible experiences. The song cannot permanently heal mental scars, but it can soothe them for a time. The subject does not suffer from any negative emotion- or mind-based Conditions that he is suffering from until the next moon phase, unless they are resolved before the Facet ends.<br /> <br /> Performing the Facet once in a given lunar phase is a breaking point for the werewolf at a -3 penalty. The power helps to center his dual nature even as it soothes the soul of his target. If he's cleaving to the World of Flesh, the breaking point is one towards Spirit. The same is true vice versa. Other werewolves who hear the song also experience the breaking point if they are hearing it for the first time in a given phase.<br /> <br /> <u>Exceptional Success:</u> Successes are gained; if the total reaches 30 successes or more, the song is particularly potent. The werewolf and all witnesses to his performance regain a point of Willpower for every success above 30.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T10:17:53-08:00","id":819349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=818865#post818865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, I went for a different concept. What do you think?<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b><u>One Voice</u> (oo)<br /> Cost:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Permanent<br /> With this Facet, a Cahalith can keep packmates in constant contact with one another. Pack members within a radius of 10 feet per dot of the Cahalith per dot of her Glory Renown are capable of instantaneous mental communication with one another. Any speaker can reach one particular packmate of his choice, or with all of them simultaneously. Connected characters also gain a bonus equal to the Cahalith's Glory on Initiative and on teamwork actions with one another, as they're better able to coordinate their efforts. The Facet cannot be used to communicate with packmates across the Gauntlet, or in a different plane of existence.</div> </div> </div> </div>As much as a like the concept of this Facet, I can't see a strong connection between dreaming and pack-coordination. How do you feel this fits within the Dreaming Moon theme?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T04:30:43-08:00","id":819761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BinAly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=819349#post819349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As much as a like the concept of this Facet, I can't see a strong connection between dreaming and pack-coordination. How do you feel this fits within the Dreaming Moon theme?</div> </div> </div> </div>When I was thinking about the themes of Dreaming Moon, I was thinking of how dreams are regarded in supernatural circles as mediums of communication, and not just foresight and prophecy. My reasoning behind making One Voice the possible two-dot Facet of the Gift is that it should allow the pack to better coordinate their activities mind-to-mind. Think of it as something similar to the concept of the Drift from Pacific Rim.<br /> <br /> That said, I'm putting it on the Gift post for the time being. And am open to any suggestions and revisions for making it more appropriate to the theme of the Dreaming Moon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T07:00:04-08:00","id":819789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=819761#post819761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When I was thinking about the themes of Dreaming Moon, I was thinking of how dreams are regarded in supernatural circles as mediums of communication, and not just foresight and prophecy. My reasoning behind making One Voice the possible two-dot Facet of the Gift is that it should allow the pack to better coordinate their activities mind-to-mind. Think of it as something similar to the concept of the Drift from Pacific Rim.<br /> <br /> That said, I'm putting it on the Gift post for the time being. And am open to any suggestions and revisions for making it more appropriate to the theme of the Dreaming Moon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough, it's a sound reasoning, just a little far from dreaming for my tastes. I will put some suggestions that might appeal to you, even for the other Facets:<ul><li><b>Sleep Deprival</b> - Affect the dreams of the prey in a way that prohibits rest and Willpower recovery, causing the prey to fear sleeping as the predator is always in her dreams.</li> <li><b>Postpone Sleep</b> - Allows the user to act for long periods without sleeping, removing penalties.</li> <li><b>Sleep Boost</b> - Could allow the character to receive the effects of a full-night sleep in just a couple hours.</li> <li><b>Guaranteed Rest</b> - The user is able to remove penalties prohibiting sleep.</li> <li><b>Dream Transportation</b> - The user is able to travel within the mind of sleeping prey, emerging at another location, as long as there are sleeping people nearby.</li> <li><b>Dream Shaping</b> - The user could gain a boost to Social Maneuvering by planting seeds into the mind of sleeping prey, Inception like.</li> <li><b>Force Sleep</b> - The user can add penalties to the prey, making it feel like she is awake for far too long, forcing and early rest.</li> <li><b>Sleeping Beauty</b> - The user would be able to trap prey into an unending slumber, until prerequisites are met. (maybe works better as a Rite)</li> <li><b>Hibernation</b> - The user would set himself into hibernation, being able to withstand harsh environments, lack of food and water, until conditions are better.</li> <li><b>Nocturnal Gatherings</b> - The whole pack always meet in their dreams, securing a territory into the Astral Realms, regardless of distance. The user could be able to upgrade this &quot;Astral Den&quot;, making it allow faster rest, removing mental conditions while inside the Den, and any other thing that helps better communication and rest.</li> <li><b>Nightmare Into Reality</b> - The user can reach into the mind of the prey and materialize it's worse fears.</li> <li><b>Ruler of the Sleeping</b> - The user can order sleeping people to do things for him, like puppets.</li> <li><b>Sense Sleeping</b> - The user is able to sense the current state of rest from people, and if there are sleeping prey nearby. As long as people are sleeping, the user can pinpoint their location, sleeping conditions (forced, suffering nightmares, peaceful) and health state.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T16:59:33-08:00","id":820039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BinAly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=819789#post819789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><ul><li><b>Sleep Deprival</b> - Affect the dreams of the prey in a way that prohibits rest and Willpower recovery, causing the prey to fear sleeping as the predator is always in her dreams.</li> <li><b>Postpone Sleep</b> - Allows the user to act for long periods without sleeping, removing penalties.</li> <li><b>Sleep Boost</b> - Could allow the character to receive the effects of a full-night sleep in just a couple hours.</li> <li><b>Guaranteed Rest</b> - The user is able to remove penalties prohibiting sleep.</li> <li><b>Dream Transportation</b> - The user is able to travel within the mind of sleeping prey, emerging at another location, as long as there are sleeping people nearby.</li> <li><b>Dream Shaping</b> - The user could gain a boost to Social Maneuvering by planting seeds into the mind of sleeping prey, Inception like.</li> <li><b>Force Sleep</b> - The user can add penalties to the prey, making it feel like she is awake for far too long, forcing and early rest.</li> <li><b>Sleeping Beauty</b> - The user would be able to trap prey into an unending slumber, until prerequisites are met. (maybe works better as a Rite)</li> <li><b>Hibernation</b> - The user would set himself into hibernation, being able to withstand harsh environments, lack of food and water, until conditions are better.</li> <li><b>Nocturnal Gatherings</b> - The whole pack always meet in their dreams, securing a territory into the Astral Realms, regardless of distance. The user could be able to upgrade this &quot;Astral Den&quot;, making it allow faster rest, removing mental conditions while inside the Den, and any other thing that helps better communication and rest.</li> <li><b>Nightmare Into Reality</b> - The user can reach into the mind of the prey and materialize it's worse fears.</li> <li><b>Ruler of the Sleeping</b> - The user can order sleeping people to do things for him, like puppets.</li> <li><b>Sense Sleeping</b> - The user is able to sense the current state of rest from people, and if there are sleeping prey nearby. As long as people are sleeping, the user can pinpoint their location, sleeping conditions (forced, suffering nightmares, peaceful) and health state.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. I'm liking these suggestions. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I can see some of them working as Facets for a Shadow Gift of Dreams or Slumber. Like Dream Shaping, Dream Transportation, and Nightmare Into Reality for the former. And Sense Sleeping, Ruler of the Sleeping, Sleeping Beauty, Hibernation, and maybe Sleep Boost for the latter.<br /> <br /> Nocturnal Gatherings seems like something that could work for Dreaming Moon as a five-dot Facet, especially with the perceived advantage it has. Plus, it's a step up from One Voice.<br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b><br /> Used the concept of Nocturnal Gatherings and gave it the name &quot;Hunter's Dream&quot;. The three-dot Facet now uses the name, &quot;Song of Uplifting Glory&quot;.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 01-30-2016, 09:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T07:23:36-08:00","id":820330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=820039#post820039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Used the concept of Nocturnal Gatherings and gave it the name &amp;quot;Hunter's Dream&amp;quot;. The three-dot Facet now uses the name, &amp;quot;Song of Uplifting Glory&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like your use of Hunter's Dream. The conceptual of the Cahalith being the heart of the Pack is something that should be aways present.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T07:30:42-08:00","id":820332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BinAly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=820330#post820330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like your use of Hunter's Dream. The conceptual of the Cahalith being the heart of the Pack is something that should be aways present.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Now, I just need to iron out the mechanics of the Astral Den, and it's good to go.<br /> <br /> By the way, regarding Aria of the Soul, is it alright as is? Do I amp up the Essence cost or downgrade its current effect?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T12:15:35-08:00","id":820492,"title":"","content":"Things on the agenda: working out two new Shadow Gifts based on the suggestions given by BinAly. <i>And</i> working out the three-dot Facet of the Dreaming Moon Gift.<br /> <br /> +++++<br /> <br /> <b>Gift of Dreams</b><br /> * Dream Transportation [Cunning] - The user is able to travel within the mind of sleeping prey, emerging at another location, as long as there are sleeping people nearby.<br /> * Sleep Deprival [Glory] - Affect the dreams of the prey in a way that prohibits rest and Willpower recovery, causing the prey to fear sleeping as the predator is always in her dreams.<br /> * Dream Shaping [Honor] - The user could gain a boost to Social Maneuvering by planting seeds into the mind of sleeping prey, Inception like.<br /> * Nightmare Into Reality [Purity] - The user can reach into the mind of the prey and materialize it's worse fears.<br /> * Sense Sleepers [Wisdom] - The user is able to sense the current state of rest from people, and if there are sleeping prey nearby. As long as people are sleeping, the user can pinpoint their location, sleeping conditions (forced, suffering nightmares, peaceful) and health state.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b>Gift of Slumber</b><br /> * Ruler of the Sleeping [Cunning] - The user can order sleeping people to do things for him, like puppets.<br /> * Postpone Sleep [Glory] - Allows the user to act for long periods without sleeping, removing penalties.<br /> * Guaranteed Rest [Honor] - The user is able to remove penalties prohibiting sleep.<br /> * Hibernation [Purity] - The user would set himself into hibernation, being able to withstand harsh environments, lack of food and water, until conditions are better.<br /> * Sleep Boost [Wisdom] - Could allow the character to receive the effects of a full-night sleep in just a couple hours.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T12:29:46-08:00","id":820502,"title":"","content":"And here's a possible revision of the three-dot Facet, which I might consider renaming Ardent Hunter...<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b>Ardent Hunter (ooo)<br /> Cost:</b> 1 Essence<br /> <b>Duration: </b>The full duration of Siskur-Dah<br /> A Cahalith on the Sacred Hunt does not just succeed. She excels, she inspires, she overwhelms opposition. Whenever she spends Willpower to enhance any rolls made to pursue her prey, she also benefits from the Inspired or Steadfast Condition in the modified roll. If she scores an Exceptional Success, she regains the spent Willpower, and all favorable witnesses to her prowess also gain a point of Willpower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T16:13:44-08:00","id":820631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=820502#post820502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And here's a possible revision of the three-dot Facet, which I might consider renaming Ardent Hunter...<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b>Ardent Hunter (ooo)<br /> Cost:</b> 1 Essence<br /> <b>Duration: </b>The full duration of Siskur-Dah<br /> A Cahalith on the Sacred Hunt does not just succeed. She excels, she inspires, she overwhelms opposition. Whenever she spends Willpower to enhance any rolls made to pursue her prey, she also benefits from the Inspired or Steadfast Condition in the modified roll. If she scores an Exceptional Success, she regains the spent Willpower, and all favorable witnesses to her prowess also gain a point of Willpower.</div> </div> </div> </div>You see, this is a place that enhancing bonuses from resting might work. Your take feels very Glorious, but has nothing of dreams about it. What if, following your focus on uniting the Pack (One Voice), the Cahalith could rest for them all? By dreaming and receiving prophecies from the Dreaming Moon, the Cahalith can allow his packmates to skip resting and still benefit from it.<br /> <br /> As long as the Cahalith rests, every pack member receives Willpower from resting and does not suffer from sleep deprivation. On top of that, each pack member receives a point of Essence as the Dreaming Moon's power penetrates the pack through the Cahalith.<br /> <br /> Also, it could boost the main power from the Auspice by adding the Cahalith's Glory to the modifier following a prophetic dream.<br /> --<br /> <br /> On Aria of the Soul, I'm a bit torn about it. I like the mechanics and the adaptation from the 1e power, but doesn't it feel a bit like a Rite by 2e standards?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T17:09:00-08:00","id":820648,"title":"","content":"I don't feel like resting is something that should emphasize on the Sacred Hunt gift. Considering the rite stops working when you do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T17:35:09-08:00","id":820654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=820648#post820648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't feel like resting is something that should emphasize on the Sacred Hunt gift. Considering the rite stops working when you do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Arguable. 'The pack breaks off the <i>Siskur-Dah</i> by taking any significant actions towards ends other than the hunt.' Taking a two-week vacation to Tahiti - hunt ending. Resting to revitalise your pack and strengthen them for the upcoming confrontation - part of the hunt, and the hunt continues. This is especially true if (under this hypothetical Gift) the Cahalith's entire purpose in resting is empowering the rest of the pack to continue the hunt. In that case, she's specifically performing a significant action in pursuit of the hunt.<br /> <br /> (Not that I'm commenting on the merits or otherwise of the suggested Gift. Just that the pack can rest within reason and not have the hunt instantly end.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T18:06:29-08:00","id":820665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BinAly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=820631#post820631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You see, this is a place that enhancing bonuses from resting might work. Your take feels very Glorious, but has nothing of dreams about it. What if, following your focus on uniting the Pack (One Voice), the Cahalith could rest for them all? By dreaming and receiving prophecies from the Dreaming Moon, the Cahalith can allow his packmates to skip resting and still benefit from it.<br /> <br /> As long as the Cahalith rests, every pack member receives Willpower from resting and does not suffer from sleep deprivation. On top of that, each pack member receives a point of Essence as the Dreaming Moon's power penetrates the pack through the Cahalith.<br /> <br /> Also, it could boost the main power from the Auspice by adding the Cahalith's Glory to the modifier following a prophetic dream.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=820648#post820648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't feel like resting is something that should emphasize on the Sacred Hunt gift. Considering the rite stops working when you do.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=820654#post820654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Arguable. 'The pack breaks off the <i>Siskur-Dah</i> by taking any significant actions towards ends other than the hunt.' Taking a two-week vacation to Tahiti - hunt ending. Resting to revitalise your pack and strengthen them for the upcoming confrontation - part of the hunt, and the hunt continues. This is especially true if (under this hypothetical Gift) the Cahalith's entire purpose in resting is empowering the rest of the pack to continue the hunt. In that case, she's specifically performing a significant action in pursuit of the hunt.<br /> <br /> (Not that I'm commenting on the merits or otherwise of the suggested Gift. Just that the pack can rest within reason and not have the hunt instantly end.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> These are all good points. The hunt doesn't end just like that when you decide to take a moment to rest for the night. That said, may shelve Ardent Hunter for a future Gift of the Glorious/Pregnant/Radiant Moon. So, what would this conceptual three-dot Facet be called, then? Should it just add a dice bonus equal to Glory on the Prophetic Dreams blessing? Or could it <i>increase</i> the number of times you may avail the benefits of the Auspice power by the Cahalith's glory (during the Hunt)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T18:07:50-08:00","id":820666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BinAly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=820631#post820631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On Aria of the Soul, I'm a bit torn about it. I like the mechanics and the adaptation from the 1e power, but doesn't it feel a bit like a Rite by 2e standards?</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps. But aren't certain Shadow Gift Facets (namely some in the Gift of Weather) also treated as Extended Actions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T20:36:06-08:00","id":820705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=820654#post820654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Arguable. 'The pack breaks off the <i>Siskur-Dah</i> by taking any significant actions towards ends other than the hunt.' Taking a two-week vacation to Tahiti - hunt ending. Resting to revitalise your pack and strengthen them for the upcoming confrontation - part of the hunt, and the hunt continues. This is especially true if (under this hypothetical Gift) the Cahalith's entire purpose in resting is empowering the rest of the pack to continue the hunt. In that case, she's specifically performing a significant action in pursuit of the hunt.<br /> <br /> (Not that I'm commenting on the merits or otherwise of the suggested Gift. Just that the pack can rest within reason and not have the hunt instantly end.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Still, sleeping it off doesn't seems evocative enough for a third rank. Sue me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T21:00:07-08:00","id":820716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=820705#post820705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Still, sleeping it off doesn't seems evocative enough for a third rank. Sue me.</div> </div> </div> </div>How about this for the Facet?<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Farsighted Hunter</u> (ooo)<br /> Cost</b>: 1 Essence<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Duration:</b> The full duration of Siskur-Dah.<br /> To be a Cahalith is to be ridden by one's dreams, to sense things in sharp context, to have one's soul constantly churning with thoughts and impulses that demand expression. In the Hunt, her visions take a sharper focus, helping her to better guide her pack towards their prey. For the duration of the Facet, when invoking Waking Visions to peer into the future, the Cahalith may gain a number of insights on her prey equal to her Glory Renown. She may also spend a point of Essence once per night to receive a Prophetic Dream regarding the prey.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T21:08:50-08:00","id":820721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=820705#post820705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Still, sleeping it off doesn't seems evocative enough for a third rank. Sue me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dial back the hostility Ephsy. Your opinion is valid. The rules you cited to back up your opinion didn't lend themselves to the black-or-white interpretation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T22:10:16-08:00","id":820744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=820721#post820721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dial back the hostility Ephsy. Your opinion is valid. The rules you cited to back up your opinion didn't lend themselves to the black-or-white interpretation.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So, any thoughts on Far-Sighted Hunter?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 02-01-2016, 01:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T00:09:01-08:00","id":820795,"title":"","content":"Slotted in Far-Sighted Hunter as the three-dot Facet for the Dreaming Moon Gift. Putting up a new Moon Gift for the Cahalith, now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T00:10:21-08:00","id":820796,"title":"","content":"<u><b><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Gift of the Ardent Moon</span></span></b></u><br /> <br /> <b><u>Siren Howl</u> (o)</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Essence<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Scene<br /> The Cahalith lets out a howl that echoes with primal power, compelling many who hear to seek out the source. All characters who hear the howl must make a successful Resolve + Composure roll, penalized by the Werewolf's Glory dots, or suffer the Lured Condition for the scene. A dramatic failure on this roll also inflicts the Obsession Condition tied to investigating the howl.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>(oo)</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Ardent Hunter (ooo)<br /> Cost:</b> 1 Essence<br /> <b>Duration: </b>The full duration of Siskur-Dah<br /> A Cahalith on the Sacred Hunt does not just succeed. She excels, she inspires, she overwhelms opposition. Whenever she spends Willpower to enhance any rolls made to pursue her prey, she also benefits from the Inspired or Steadfast Condition in the modified roll. If she scores an Exceptional Success, she regains the spent Willpower, and all favorable witnesses to her prowess also gain a point of Willpower.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Drawing The Curtain</u> (oooo)</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3 Essence<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Manipulation + Expression + Glory vs. the subject's Composure + Primal Urge<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Duration:</b> 1 Roll per success<br /> A wise storyteller knows that when an enemy must be dealt with, the best story is a tragedy. Cahalith with this Facet can tell a tale of woe so terrible that the subject of the tale is marked by fate for an awful end.<br /> <br /> <u>Dramatic Failure</u>: Not only does the story not stir fate to turn on the listener, but the listener is aware that the Cahalith was toying with his destiny.<br /> <br /> <u>Failure</u>: The Cahalith finishes her story, but nothing happens.<br /> <br /> <u>Success</u>: The story influences the listener in a dark way. The next time the listener's player (or Storyteller) chooses to spend Willpower to add dice to a roll, tragedy strikes. The Cahalith's player may declare that the roll is automatically considered a dramatic failure.<br /> <br /> <u>Exceptional Success</u>: As a success, but the prey receives the Demoralized Condition after suffering from the effects of the Facet for the first time.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Magnum Opus </u>(ooooo)</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>3 Essence<br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b>Presence + Expression + Glory<br /> <b>Action: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Duration:</b> 1 Roll Per Success<br /> Stories serve a number of functions for a pack: To remind them of past glories, educate, or inspire to future greatness. The inspirational potential of the story is demonstrated at its full potential with this Facet. The storyteller weaves an epic tale of how spectacular their successes will be in the near future, and the listeners are so inspired they are able to perform acts with success beyond their wildest dreams. The Cahalith can use this Facet to affect several listeners equal to her Glory + Primal Urge.<br /> <br /> <u>Dramatic Failure:</u> The story's effect is counter to the intention. The next time the listener spends Willpower to enhance a roll, no dice are added to the roll, and the listener still loses the point.<br /> <br /> <u>Failure:</u> The Facet has no effect.<br /> <br /> <u>Success:</u> The story rouses greatness in its listener. The next time the listener spends Willpower to enhance an action, instead of adding three dice to the roll, add three successes to the total rolled.<br /> <br /> <u>Exceptional Success:</u> The next time the listener spends a point of Willpower to enhance an action, that action is automatically an exceptional success.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 03-10-2017, 07:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T02:53:46-08:00","id":820853,"title":"","content":"<u><b><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Gift of Dreams</span></span></span></b></u><br /> <br /> <b><u>Dream Journey</u> [Cunning]</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Essence<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Wits + Occult + Cunning<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> By tapping into the spiritual resonance of dreams, the Uratha can travel to another location as long as there are sleeping individuals nearby.<br /> <br /> <u>Dramatic Failure:</u> The Facet not only fails to take effect, but it also leaves the werewolf greatly disoriented. He suffers the Confused Condition.<br /> <br /> <u>Failure:</u> The Facet fails to take effect.<br /> <br /> <u>Success:</u> The werewolf enters the dreamscape and may use it to instantaneously traverse physical distances. The physical distance traveled is not greater than 10 miles per dot in his Cunning Renown. He emerges as close as possible to the physical place of his choosing, within the general vicinity of the closest sleeper.<br /> <br /> <u>Exceptional Success:</u> As a success, but the werewolf emerges exactly where he wants to be, regardless of whether or not there is a sleeper nearby.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Phantom Menace</u> [Glory]<br /> Cost:</b> 3 Essence<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Presence + Occult + Glory vs. Composure + Primal Urge<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> The werewolf can reach into the mind of the prey and materialize his worse fears.<br /> <br /> <u>Dramatic Failure:</u> The Facet's energies rebound on the werewolf, harrowing his soul and leaving him drained. He receives the Soul Shocked Condition.<br /> <br /> <u>Failure:</u> The Facet fails to summon the prey's worst fears.<br /> <br /> <u>Success:</u> The werewolf creates an ephemeral being that embodies the greatest horrors in the prey's psyche. This entity has a Rank equal to the werewolf's Glory Renown, and is created as a Dream Form using the target's Mental Attributes as a basis.<br /> <br /> <u>Exceptional Success:</u> As a success, but the dream entity now uses the highest of the target's Power, Finesse, and Resistance Attributes to determine its own. Furthermore, being confronted with one's worst fears inflicts the Soul Shocked Condition on the target.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Inception</u> [Honor]<br /> Cost:</b> 1 Essence<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Manipulation + Empathy + Honor vs. Composure + Primal Urge<br /> <b>Action:</b> Extended (5 Successes; each roll represents 1 minute)<br /> <b>Duration:</b> 1 Week<br /> By seeding suggestions into the minds of his sleeping prey, the werewolf may exert a greater influence upon him through interactions in the waking world. This Facet can only be performed within sight of the target while he is asleep or otherwise unconscious.<br /> <br /> <u>Dramatic Failure:</u> The Facet overwhelms the target's subconscious with horrific visions that paint the werewolf in a negative light. He receives the Frightened Condition towwards him, which persists until the next sunrise.<br /> <br /> <u>Failure:</u> The Uratha fails to accumulate any successes, and gains the Stumbled Condition.<br /> <br /> <u>Success:</u> For the duration of the Facet, the werewolf adds his Honor Renown as a bonus to all rolls made to conduct Social Maneuvering with the target.<br /> <br /> <u>Exceptional Success:</u> In addition to the effects of a success, the werewolf raises his first impression by one step, and may inflict the Obsession Condition upon his prey with regards to helping him upon successfully opening the final Door.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Lunatic Pandora</u> [Purity]</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3 Essence<br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b>Stamina + Survival + Purity - Composure<br /> <b>Action: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Scene<br /> By directing a horrific howl upon a target of this Facet, the werewolf inflicts harrowing sensations upon his prey's psyche.<br /> <br /> <u>Dramatic Failure:</u> Not only did the howl fail to harrow the Facet's target. It had the unfortunate benefit of steeling his resolve. The target instead gains the Steadfast Condition.<br /> <br /> <u>Failure:</u> The Facet has no effect on the target.<br /> <br /> <u>Success:</u> The howl strikes into the victim's mind, triggering a rush of random hallucinations which leaves him stunned where he stands. He suffers the Confused Condition.<br /> <br /> <u>Exceptional Success:</u> As a success, but the victim also receives the Stunned Tilt.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Sense the Sleepers</u> [Wisdom]<br /> Cost:</b> 1 Essence<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Wits + Empathy + Wisdom<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Scene<br /> The werewolf opens her senses to the world around her, getting a sense for the sleeping and dreaming minds that might be nearby.<br /> <br /> <u>Dramatic Failure:</u> The werewolf is suddenly afflicted with a wave of drowsiness, which sends him into a trance-like state. He gains the Insensate Tilt for the scene.<br /> <br /> <u>Failure:</u> The werewolf is unable to tell whether anyone is sleeping in her vicinity. He may choose to try again within the scene at a cumulative -1 penalty (up to a maximum of -5).<br /> <br /> <u>Success:</u> The werewolf can accurately count the number of sleeping creatures larger than a cat within a range of 10 yards per dot of Wisdom Renown, and can sense the rough location and size of each. He may also determine both their sleeping condition (forced, suffering nightmares, peaceful) and overall health.<br /> <br /> <u>Exceptional Success:</u> As above, but the range of the Facet is doubled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 03-11-2017, 06:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"