uture-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T13:31:35-08:00","id":821172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=821170#post821170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe. Remind me what is the function of the gift as intented? I know it's for Gibbous moons but I don't know much else</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. It's for Gibbous Moons. Still have to figure out what the overall theme is but the Ardent Hunter Facet should give me a rough idea soon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T19:26:15-08:00","id":821375,"title":"","content":"Radiant Moon sounds like a Full Moon to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T21:46:34-08:00","id":821437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=821375#post821375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Radiant Moon sounds like a Full Moon to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>You got any suggestions? I have a few possibilities - Ardent Moon (referencing the three-dot Facet), Blazing Moon, or Glorious Moon, <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T21:49:44-08:00","id":821441,"title":"","content":"A look in the thesaurus suggested 'Crooked' as an alternative for Gibbous. Crooked Moon has a certain ring to it.<br /> <br /> First edition went more with the concepts attached. Witch's Moon, Judge's Moon, Dreamer's Moon. You could probably shake up the formula, 'Skald's Sky' or 'Seer's Silver.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-02-2016, 12:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T22:05:34-08:00","id":821446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=821441#post821441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A look in the thesaurus suggested 'Crooked' as an alternative for Gibbous. Crooked Moon has a certain ring to it.<br /> <br /> First edition went more with the concepts attached. Witch's Moon, Judge's Moon, Dreamer's Moon. You could probably shake up the formula, 'Skald's Sky' or 'Seer's Silver.'</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll go with Crooked Moon, for the time being, then.<br /> <br /> Skald's Sky or Seer's Silver sound like very nice names for Facets, if you ask me. Though perhaps Skald's Moon could work, too? Or how about Bardic Moon?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 02-02-2016, 01:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T22:22:17-08:00","id":821450,"title":"","content":"In-progress conversion of the Scheherezade Gifts, Drawing the Curtain and Magnum Opus, for Crooked Moon. Any suggestions for reskinning them are welcome.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Drawing The Curtain</u> (oooo)</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3 Essence<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Manipulation + Expression + Glory vs. the subject's Composure + Primal Urge<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Duration:</b> One roll per success<br /> A wise storyteller knows that when an enemy must be dealt with, the best story is a tragedy. Cahalith with this Facet can tell a tale of woe so terrible that the subject of the tale is marked by fate for an awful end.<br /> <br /> <u>Dramatic Failure</u>: Not only does the story not stir fate to turn on the listener, but the listener is aware that the Cahalith was toying with his destiny.<br /> <br /> <u>Failure</u>: The Cahalith finishes her story, but nothing happens.<br /> <br /> <u>Success</u>: The story influences the listener in a dark way. The next time the listener's player (or Storyteller) chooses to spend Willpower to add dice to a roll, tragedy strikes. The Cahalith's player may declare that the roll is automatically considered a dramatic failure. <br /> <br /> <u>Exceptional Success</u>: As a success, but the prey receives the Demoralized Condition after suffering from the effects of the Facet for the first time.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Magnum Opus </u>(ooooo)</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>3 Essence<br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b>Presence + Expression + Glory<br /> <b>Action: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Duration:</b> 1 roll Per Success<br /> Stories serve a number of functions for a pack: To remind them of past glories, educate, or inspire to future greatness. The inspirational potential of the story is demonstrated at its full potential with this Facet. The storyteller weaves an epic tale of how spectacular their successes will be in the near future, and the listeners are so inspired they are able to perform acts with success beyond their wildest dreams. The Cahalith can use this Facet to affect several listeners equal to her Glory + Primal Urge.<br /> <br /> <u>Dramatic Failure:</u> The story's effect is counter to the intention. The next time the listener spends Willpower to enhance a roll, no dice are added to the roll, and the listener still loses the point.<br /> <br /> <u>Failure:</u> The Facet has no effect.<br /> <br /> <u>Success:</u> The story rouses greatness in its listener. The next time the listener spends Willpower to enhance an action, instead of adding three dice to the roll, add three successes to the total rolled. <br /> <br /> <u>Exceptional Success:</u> The next time the listener spends a point of Willpower to enhance an action, that action is automatically an exceptional success.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T07:34:59-07:00","id":905620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=750715#post750715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u><span style=\"font-size:26px\">Gift of Savagery</span></u><br /> At its heart, a predator is a savage creature. And the Uratha are no exception. Those who seek to master the Gift of Savagery take this primal truth, and shape it into another tool in their hunts. Among the Pure, Predator Kings are masters at controlling their feral instincts and manipulating such savagery in others. Those with this Gift become more capable killers, and even more lethal foes in a hunt. Similarly, Blood Talons who have had the Gift marked upon their bodies are counted among the most vicious of their tribe. And more than once have they felled prey who made the mistake of underestimating their ferocity. <hr /><br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Unshackled Rage</u> [Honor]</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Essence per target<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Manipulation + Expression + Honor vs. Composure + Primal Urge<br /> <b>Action:</b> Contested; resistance is considered reflexive<br /> With this Facet, the Predator King has mastered his own savagery and anger to the point where he can fiercely project it onto others, making them experience the depths of his potential for viciousness. More than that, he can focus his anger so powerfully that it can steal the rational thoughts of humans and other werewolves, causing humans to act like savage animals, and pushing Uratha close to Kuruth.<br /> <br /> <u>Dramatic Failure:</u> The attempted projection of the character's killing urges backfires, and he must test for Death Rage.<br /> <br /> <u>Failure:</u> The Gift has no effect.<br /> <br /> <u>Success:</u> The minds of the targets are clouded in animalist fury, making people act on their most savage instincts. Each individual targeted suffers the following effects depending on their nature.<br /> <br /> Werewolves must roll for Death Rage, and treat their effective Harmony as one step lower for the purpose of resisting Death Rage stimuli for the scene.<br /> <br /> Humans become violently angry with the closest person to them (including the werewolf if appropriate). They suffer the effects of the Berserk Condition for the remainder of the scene.<br /> <br /> <u>Exceptional Success:</u> As with a success, though a werewolf affected by the Facet falls into Wasu-Im on the spot. Furthermore, the effects now last a number of scenes equal to the werewolf's Honor Renown.</div> </div> </div> </div>-=-<br /> <br /> I was thinking of using this Gift in a game I'm in, but I realized this facet has some major overlap with the Cunning Facet of the Gift of Rage. Very nearly identical.<br /> <br /> I was thinking of replacing it with some kind of gift that gives you your Honor in turns after your last health box fills with aggravated damage, sort of a last ditch effort that seems very Predator King, even if it's not terribly useful for a player character it could also allow for some cool RP moments.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I just figured I'd mention it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","user":"Amravanti","date":". 06-02-2016, 02:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T13:08:33-07:00","id":905899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=905620#post905620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking of using this Gift in a game I'm in, but I realized this facet has some major overlap with the Cunning Facet of the Gift of Rage. Very nearly identical.<br /> <br /> I was thinking of replacing it with some kind of gift that gives you your Honor in turns after your last health box fills with aggravated damage, sort of a last ditch effort that seems very Predator King, even if it's not terribly useful for a player character it could also allow for some cool RP moments.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I just figured I'd mention it.</div> </div> </div> </div>How is this for an alternative?<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Unshackled Rage</u> [Honor]<br /> Cost:</b> Special (See Below)<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Permanent<br /> With this Facet, the Werewolf has mastered his own savagery and anger to the point where he can draw out his time in Gauru, allowing him more opportunities to make his enemies experience the depths of his viciousness. Whenever he rolls his Resolve + Composure after being in Gauru form for the maximum number of turns, he also receives extra turns equal to his Honor Renown on a success. Once this additional time has been spent, he may choose to spend Essence as a reflexive action to extend this further by a number of turns equal to the points spent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T17:20:57-07:00","id":906062,"title":"","content":"I don't know, because again doesn't that just seem like a mirror of another Rage Facet? (Honor). And since Predator Kings also get that gift as affinity it seems like overkill.<br /> <br /> And honestly, it just seems like Savagery should veer away from just being Rage 2.0 and focus more on being a terrifying/horrifying battle beast (with less focus on Garou form), though how exactly that is achieved I don't know. That's my take, anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","user":"Amravanti","date":". 06-02-2016, 08:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T17:47:43-07:00","id":906082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=906062#post906062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know, because again doesn't that just seem like a mirror of another Rage Facet? (Honor). And since Predator Kings also get that gift as affinity it seems like overkill.<br /> <br /> And honestly, it just seems like Savagery should veer away from just being Rage 2.0 and focus more on being a terrifying/horrifying battle beast (with less focus on Garou form), though how exactly that is achieved I don't know. That's my take, anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, 2E Werewolf allows you to get an extra turn in Gauru beyond the limits of your Stamina + Primal Urge if you succeed in a Resolve + Composure roll, by default. What I was aiming for with that version of Unshackled Rage is that it increases the number of such additional turns, while also giving an option of spending Essence to continue pushing beyond that. Though seeing as it <i>does</i> mimic Perfected Rage in the extra turns somewhat, perhaps the Essence expenditure could do the trick somehow?<br /> <br /> Or maybe I could look again at Armory Reloaded's War Form gamble for ideas in revising the Facet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T11:25:40-07:00","id":908456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=906082#post906082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, 2E Werewolf allows you to get an extra turn in Gauru beyond the limits of your Stamina + Primal Urge if you succeed in a Resolve + Composure roll, by default. What I was aiming for with that version of Unshackled Rage is that it increases the number of such additional turns, while also giving an option of spending Essence to continue pushing beyond that. Though seeing as it <i>does</i> mimic Perfected Rage in the extra turns somewhat, perhaps the Essence expenditure could do the trick somehow?<br /> <br /> Or maybe I could look again at Armory Reloaded's War Form gamble for ideas in revising the Facet.</div> </div> </div> </div>How about it gives them a bonus on Resolve + Composure rolls to maintain control. Show that they can control the rage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T12:37:06-07:00","id":908519,"title":"","content":"How about it gives you the gauru Rage and Tooth and Claw bonuses and mind shielding, but not the healing, for use in any form. Sort of like a pseudo-Kuruth. You can even have it treat gifts that are activated during Kuruth or cost nothing during Kuruth as if they were in death rage. You can manage it for Stamina + Primal Urge + Renown for the facet.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T18:20:14-07:00","id":908774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=908456#post908456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How about it gives them a bonus on Resolve + Composure rolls to maintain control. Show that they can control the rage.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=908519#post908519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about it gives you the gauru Rage and Tooth and Claw bonuses and mind shielding, but not the healing, for use in any form. Sort of like a pseudo-Kuruth. You can even have it treat gifts that are activated during Kuruth or cost nothing during Kuruth as if they were in death rage. You can manage it for Stamina + Primal Urge + Renown for the facet.</div> </div> </div> </div>The bonus to Resolve + Composure seems a bit underwhelming, especially since all you get out of it is <i>one</i> turn. Unless you're thinking of making the Facet add dots in Honor Renown to all Resolve + Composure rolls, specifically the ones made to avoid falling into Kuruth, then maybe that works. The question, now, is whether or not there's already such a Facet in existence in Werewolf 2E.<br /> <br /> Giving the Rage, Tooth and Claw bonuses, and mind shielding might be a bit over the top in my opinion. Moreso when you add in the free cost for Facets that automatically trigger during Death Rage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T05:57:28-08:00","id":1059457,"title":"","content":"Minor update: added an Exceptional Success effect to the one-dot Facet of the Gift of the Lying Moon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T07:04:18-08:00","id":1059482,"title":"","content":"Finally worked out a one-dot Facet for the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=820796#post820796\">Bardic Moon Gift</a>. I'm also thinking of weaving in the Awestruck Condition as part of the two-dot Facet. As always, critique and suggestions are welcome.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Siren Howl</u> (o)</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Essence<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Scene<br /> The Cahalith lets out a howl that echoes with primal power, compelling many who hear to seek out the source. All characters who hear the howl must make a successful Resolve + Composure roll, penalized by the Werewolf's Glory dots, or suffer the Lured Condition for the scene. A dramatic failure on this roll also inflicts the Obsession Condition tied to investigating the howl.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 03-07-2017, 10:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-10T16:58:44-08:00","id":1061072,"title":"","content":"Renamed the Gift of the Bardic Moon to the Gift of the Ardent Moon. Also working on its two-dot Facet at last.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T03:56:06-08:00","id":1061191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=906062#post906062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know, because again doesn't that just seem like a mirror of another Rage Facet? (Honor). And since Predator Kings also get that gift as affinity it seems like overkill.<br /> <br /> And honestly, it just seems like Savagery should veer away from just being Rage 2.0 and focus more on being a terrifying/horrifying battle beast (with less focus on Garou form), though how exactly that is achieved I don't know. That's my take, anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=908519#post908519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about it gives you the gauru Rage and Tooth and Claw bonuses and mind shielding, but not the healing, for use in any form. Sort of like a pseudo-Kuruth. You can even have it treat gifts that are activated during Kuruth or cost nothing during Kuruth as if they were in death rage. You can manage it for Stamina + Primal Urge + Renown for the facet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Finally got back to this after all this time. Here's an alternative Facet I thought up.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Savage Mind</u> [Honor]</b><br /> <b>Duration:</b> Permanent<br /> The werewolf bears his feral nature in all forms, and this Facet shapes it into a shield against whatever compulsion would dissuade him. Whenever he shifts into Dalu, Urshul, or Urhan, all rolls made to supernaturally influence his thoughts or emotions suffer a penalty equal to his Honor Renown. If he is in Hisshu, he applies half this, rounded up. If he is in Gauru, though, all attempts inflict the penalty as bashing damage instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 03-11-2017, 11:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}